window.MONARCH_CHAPTERS=(window.MONARCH_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":176,"title":"Chapter 176: Practical Exam (1)","paragraphs":["The day of the semester examination finally arrived.","More than four hundred first-year students gathered inside the massive Gateway Hall of Novaris Academy.","The atmosphere was far more serious than usual.","Rows upon rows of students stood neatly in formation while enormous teleportation gates hummed with magical energy at the front of the hall. Blue runes glowed across the metal structures, illuminating the area with a faint light.","Every student had been provided with academy-issued battle gear.","The uniform consisted of black, white, and blue combat attire designed for mobility and protection. Most students also carried backpacks containing emergency supplies and rations.","Some looked excited. Some looked nervous. Others appeared eager for battle.","Noah stood among Class A-1 while observing the crowd around him.","Nearby, he could spot familiar faces.","Damien stood calmly with his arms crossed.","Lyria looked slightly nervous.","Leonard appeared excited.","Kaelan looked serious for this exam.","Emma was bored as if she didn’t want to give this exam.","Arisha was as cool as ever.","Then he looked at other class.","B-2, where Ragnar and Draven were present.","Draven looked serious for once. Even Ragnar seemed unusually tense.","At the front stood the instructors.","Victor, he was head instructor of class A-2, Lucia, of Class B-1, Atticus of class B-2 and lastly Morgana.","The four instructors watched over the students as the teleportation gates continued operating. After several minutes, Morgana stepped forward. Her sharp eyes swept across the crowd.","The entire hall became silent immediately.","\"Alright, students,\" she said in a loud and authoritative voice. \"Move through the portal in an orderly line.\"","One by one, students began entering the teleportation gates.","Bright flashes of light appeared every few seconds.","Soon Noah’s turn arrived. Without hesitation, he stepped through the portal. A wave of spatial energy washed over him. His vision blurred briefly.","Then the world around him changed. He could feel some weird tickling. Noah emerged into an open clearing surrounded by an enormous forest.","The first thing he noticed was the size of the trees. They were gigantic. Each trunk was so massive that dozens of people could stand side by side around it. Some trees reached heights comparable to thirty-story buildings.","Their enormous canopies covered the sky like a green ocean.","Noah immediately noticed the difference. Just weeks ago, they had completed monster hunting practice in the forests near Oakhaven City.","But this place felt completely different.","This one looks older and it was wilder. More dangerous. A temporary base had been established in the clearing.","Numerous tents filled the area. Large magical machines operated continuously. Staff members moved around while checking equipment and monitoring magical screens.","Several additional instructors could also be seen maintaining security. Most likely, the academy had spent days preparing this location.","Even a stable portal gate had been installed.","’They’ve definitely been setting this place up since yesterday,’ Noah thought while looking around. ’Transporting hundreds of students isn’t something they could do in a few hours.’","Soon all the students arrived through the portals.","The four instructors followed shortly afterward.","Everyone gathered once again into organized rows.","Murmurs spread through the crowd as students looked around curiously. Where exactly were they? What kind of exam awaited them? Everyone were curious about what would be this race exactly about.","After giving everyone enough time to settle down, Morgana stepped forward.","Her voice echoed throughout the clearing.","\"So, you’re all wondering where we are right now.\"","The students nodded immediately.","Morgana pointed toward the endless forest.","\"We are currently on a remote place located far from any major civilization. No intelligent races live here. No humans or any other race live here.\"","She paused. \"Only monsters.\"","A wave of whispers immediately spread through the crowd. Some students became nervous.","Others looked excited.","Morgana raised a hand. The murmuring instantly stopped.","\"Relax all of you.\"","Her voice remained calm.","\"The academy has already surveyed this forest name Gloomspire Thicket extensively. We have removed or captured all threats exceeding D+ Rank.\"","\"The strongest monsters remaining here are D+ Rank creatures. Most of you will never encounter one. Also before this the strongest monsters in area where race will be held was B rank monsters.\"","The students visibly relaxed after hearing that.","Then Morgana continued.","\"Now listen carefully. This semester examination will consist of a live-combat survival race.\"","Her words immediately regained everyone’s full attention. A large magical screen appeared behind her. Information began appearing across its surface.","\"The southern region of this forest will serve as your starting area. You will be teleported individually to random locations throughout the southern perimeter.\"","She pointed toward a glowing marker displayed on the map.","\"Your objective is simple. Travel across the forest and reach the North Beacon located at the opposite side of the forest. You all must go in one direction..\"","The screen zoomed outward, revealing the enormous distance between the starting area and the destination.","Many students frowned.","The journey looked much longer than expected.","Morgana continued.","\"The examination will run continuously for forty-eight hours. Two full days. You are permitted to carry your academy-issued weapon, potions, and your two-day ration pack.mWhat you do afterward is entirely your responsibility.\"","She folded her arms.","\"Manage your stamina. Find food if necessary. Build shelter if necessary. Sleep if you dare. Survive.\"","The atmosphere became increasingly serious.","Then the point system appeared on the magical screen.","\"The final rankings will be determined by points. Points may be earned through three methods.\"","A large heading appeared.","[MONSTER ELIMINATION BOUNTIES]","Morgana began explaining.","\"Points are automatically awarded when your Academy Bracelet verifies a fatal blow.\"","\"F-Rank Beast — 5 Points.\"","\"F Rank Beast — 10 Points.\"","\"F+ Rank Beast — 15 Points.\"","\"E- Rank Beast — 30 Points.\"","\"E Rank Beast — 50 Points.\"","\"E+ Rank Beast — 75 Points.\"","\"D- Rank Beast — 150 Points.\"","\"D Rank Beast - 200 Points\"","A few students looked excited.","Then Morgana added coldly,","\"D-Rank population density is extremely low. Do not go searching for them unless you are confident.\"","The next line appeared.","\"D+ Rank Beasts — 300 Points.\"","\"These are sector boss variants. High lethality risk. Fight at your own discretion. Don’t do anything stupid. \"","Many students immediately abandoned the idea of hunting them.","Morgana moved on.","The next heading appeared.","[STUDENT ENGAGEMENT PROTOCOL]","A collective murmur spread through the crowd.","PvP.","Everyone immediately understood.","\"Combat between students is authorized. To eliminate another participant, you must injured then unless their health is around 70 percent. The gear you have wore is something that will automatically teleport you to our base if your health decrease past 70 percent. The wrist band you are wearing will count your points by each kill and elimination.\"","A small crystal token hanging from every student’s waist began glowing.","\" You locations will be tracked because of the wrist band. So don’t worry about getting lost. Each elimination grants fifty points.\"","Then Morgana smiled faintly.","\"And and all points of the eliminated student’s current points will automatically transfer to the victor.\"","The crowd exploded into discussion.","Many students immediately began looking at one another differently.","Noah noticed it instantly.","The atmosphere had changed. Everyone had suddenly become a potential source of points.","Morgana waited for the noise to settle before continuing.","The final category appeared.","[ARRIVAL BONUSES]","\"First Place Arrival — Five Thousand Points.\"","A wave of excitement spread through the students.","\"Second Place Arrival — Three Thousand Points.\"","\"Third Place Arrival — Two Thousand Points.\"","\"Fourth through Tenth Place — One Thousand Points.\"","\"Eleventh through Twentieth Place — Eight Hundred Points.\"","\"Twenty-First through Fiftieth Place — Five Hundred Points.\"","Even Noah’s eyes narrowed.","The rewards were enormous.","Especially first place.","Then Morgana revealed the final rule.","\"The examination ends the exact moment the fiftieth student reaches the North Beacon.\"","Everyone became silent.","\"The instant the fiftieth arrival is recorded, the tracking system will lock. All remaining students will automatically receive a signal indicating the examination has concluded through their wrist band. In other words...\"","Her gaze swept across the crowd.","\"Being alive is not enough. You must reach the finish line before the fiftieth student. The exam could end within day if fifty students reach the end or if fifty students didn’t reach the end in two days the exam will be concluded. Also there might be monster stronger than D+ existed, run away as fast as possible. Despite you could get teleported back to base...\"","she continued. \"If monster attacked too fast like behead you or crush your head within seconds. Then you could not survive.\"","A heavy silence settled over the clearing.","The pressure suddenly felt much greater.","Morgana nodded slightly. \"So if you fought against each other don’t go for killing. So for lethal attacks that won’t kill students.\"","\"While the results of the semester examination will be released within one week after completion. We have taken care of all your safety.\"","She looked at all four hundred students.","Some appeared nervous.","Some excited.","Some eager to prove themselves.","Then a faint smile appeared on her face.","\"Prepare yourselves. In a few minutes, you will be teleported to your starting positions. And once that happens...\"","Her voice became cold. \"The exam begins.\"","Suddenly a huge magic circled appeared beneath the students. And one by one the vanished from their positions.","Noah’s vision blurred and soon he landed on unknown place.","He was no longer at the base created by academy.","He sighed. The first thing he need to do was find the north direction."]},{"number":177,"title":"Chapter 177: Practical Exam (2)","paragraphs":["Noah remained where he was and pulled out a small compass from his storage ring.","\"Good thing I bought some necessary things.\"","Noah knew there were no restrictions on what students could bring for the exam.","However, there were a few things everyone needed to keep in mind, even though the instructors had not explicitly mentioned them.","The first was artifacts. They were strictly prohibited. If an exam ever allowed artifacts, the academy would clearly state it in the rules beforehand.","The second was weapon ranking.","All students were required to use academy-issued weapons. If they wished to bring their own weapons, those weapons had to be of a low rank.","Weapons were generally ranked from G to SS.","Low Tier: G, F, E","Mid Tier: D, C, B","High Tier: A, S, SS","All first-year students currently possessed E-Rank weapons.","Even Noah’s blue-and-silver spear was only E-Rank.","The same applied to every other first-year student.","These weapons were decent, but far from magnificent.","Noah summoned his spear and held it tightly.","Even his spear was considered low-tier.","\"Once I break through to the Condensed Core Rank, I’ll try to buy a mid-tier weapon.\"","He performed a few stretches before dashing into the forest.","It was going to be a long race after all.","Soon, he ventured deeper into the forest.","’How can I top this exam?’","His footsteps crunched against the dry leaves scattered across the ground.","Stomp.","Stomp.","Stomp.","Tens of kilometers away from Noah was Damien.","He stood atop a thick tree branch overlooking the vast forest below.","His hazel eyes calmly observed the endless sea of dark-green wilderness.","\"Where is Noah? I need to defeat him before he does something out of nowhere.\"","Damien was determined to secure first place in this exam.","He had no intention of taking it easy on anyone.","Anyone who stood in his way would be defeated.","The young man leaped from the branch and dashed toward the north.","After running for quite some time, Noah encountered his first monster.","It was a Scavenger Scuttler.","Roughly the size of a large dog, the creature resembled a grotesque combination of a hairless rat and a giant beetle.","Its oily black skin stretched tightly over its frame, revealing faint gray veins beneath the surface. Long clawed limbs supported its body while a segmented tail dragged behind it.","It was alone.","The moment it sensed Noah’s presence, it turned around and attempted to flee.","Noah didn’t allow it the chance.","Mana surged through his body as he dashed forward.","A layer of sharp blue ice coated the blade of his spear.","Swung!","The spear flashed.","Splash!","Dark blood sprayed through the air.","The monster collapsed lifelessly onto the ground.","\"That was easy.\"","Noah shook the spear, flicking the blood from its blade.","\"F-Rank.\"","He glanced at the dead creature.","\"F-Rank Beast. Five points... it’s nothing special. I need to find stronger monsters and accumulate as many points as possible.\"","’Knowing Damien, he must already be killing plenty of monsters. I need to keep up.’","Without wasting time, Noah dashed deeper into the forest.","However, before he could go much farther, a strange scratching noise reached his ears.","Skkkrrr...","Skkkrrr...","Skrrr...","Chitter-chitter-chitter...","Noah immediately stopped.","His eyes narrowed as he searched for the source of the sound.","Soon he found it.","A large group of Scavenger Scuttlers emerged from the undergrowth.","There were over twenty of them.","The moment they sensed Noah’s presence, multiple pairs of glowing red eyes locked onto him.","The entire group became silent.","They simply stared.","Noah smirked.","Around him, ice rapidly condensed in the air.","One sword.","Five swords.","Ten swords.","Twenty-five swords.","A total of twenty-five ice swords floated around him.","Seeing only a single human standing before them, the monsters decided to attack.","To them, he looked like easy prey.","SCCCRREEEEECCCHHHHH!!","The entire pack screamed in unison before charging toward him.","Noah’s blue eyes remained calm.","With a simple gesture, all twenty-five ice swords shot forward.","Whistle!","Whistle!","Whistle!","The weapons tore through the air with incredible speed.","Shckk!","Shckk!","Shckk!","One after another, the swords pierced through skulls.","Dark blood splattered across the forest floor.","Most of the monsters died before they could even reach him.","The few that managed to get close were met with another attack.","Noah stomped on the ground.","Sharp ice spikes erupted upward.","Piercing.","Impaling.","Killing.","Within moments, the entire pack was dead.","\"One... two... three...\"","Noah counted the corpses.","\"Twenty-three... twenty-four including the last one.\"","A grin appeared on his face.","\"At this rate, reaching five thousand points in a single day doesn’t sound difficult.\"","His confidence rose for a moment.","Then he frowned.","\"Fuck. That means other people can do this too. Reaching the finish line only gives bonus points. Dammit.\"","Without wasting another second, he resumed running.","He didn’t even bother collecting the mana cores.","F-Rank cores were practically worthless to him.","ROOOAAARRRRRR!!","Suddenly, a thunderous roar erupted from the side.","A gigantic figure lunged toward him.","\"What the—?!\"","Noah’s eyes widened.","He immediately jumped forward.","BOOOOM!!","A massive stone club smashed into the ground where he had been standing moments earlier.","The impact shattered the earth and sent dirt flying everywhere.","\"Dammit!\"","Noah rolled across the ground before quickly regaining his footing.","The dust slowly settled.","A towering figure emerged from the cloud.","The monster stood well over three meters tall.","Its body was a mountain of muscle wrapped in dark crimson skin.","Bulging veins crawled across its massive arms while thick black fur covered portions of its shoulders and legs.","Its head belonged to a bull.","Two enormous curved horns extended from either side of its skull, sharp enough to impale a person with ease.","Its yellow eyes burned with savage intelligence.","Heavy breaths escaped its nostrils like steam from a furnace.","Every exhale produced visible bursts of hot air.","In one hand, it wielded an enormous stone club nearly as large as Noah himself.","The crude weapon was covered in cracks and dried blood.","A Minotaur."]},{"number":178,"title":"Chapter 178: Practical Exam (3)","paragraphs":["\"An E Rank... maybe even an E+ Rank monster.\"","A smile slowly appeared on Noah’s face.","\"Now that’s what I wanted to fight.\"","The Minotaur snorted heavily.","Red mana began gathering around its stone club. The weapon started radiating a faint crimson glow.","\"The fuck? It knows how to use mana on its weapon. Dammit.\"","Noah immediately assumed a battle stance.","Mana flowed through his spear.","A thin layer of compressed ice covered the blade.","A tiny frost droplet formed at its tip.","The Minotaur had already begun charging.","BOOM!","BOOM!","BOOM!","Each heavy step caused the ground to tremble.","Noah reinforced his legs and arms with mana.","Then both combatants collided.","CLANG!!","The clash echoed through the forest.","\"Argh!\"","Noah gritted his teeth.","The Minotaur’s physical strength was monstrous.","However, it was still within the limits he could handle.","After all, he was a High Awakened Core user.","The moment Noah’s spear collided with the stone club, frost rapidly spread across the weapon’s surface.","A layer of ice instantly began freezing the stone.","Noah smirked as he pushed the monster back with sheer strength.","\"ROAAARRR!\"","The Minotaur roared furiously.","The beast’s massive frame staggered backward for a moment. Its crimson skin stretched over layers of dense muscle, and its enormous bull-like head shook violently. Thick black fur covered portions of its shoulders and forearms, while its curved horns gleamed menacingly under the forest light.","Noah wasn’t intimidated by the beast at all.","Soon, a magic circle began forming in front of him.","For now, all the spells he had learned were low-ranking.","Spells were ranked from One-Star to Eight-Star.","Each Core Rank allowed a person to learn spells of the corresponding rank.","Noah was capable of learning Two-Star spells. However, because of his Ice Creation ability and his focus on weapon mastery, he had not spent much time learning additional spells.","For now, he was using Frost Mist.","The Minotaur noticed the magic circle but didn’t sense any significant danger from it.","With a furious growl, it swung its massive stone club horizontally, aiming to crush Noah.","However, at that exact moment, a freezing mist shot forward from the completed magic circle.","A dense cloud of frost engulfed the Minotaur’s entire body.","The beast immediately began shaking its body violently.","Its movements slowed.","Thin layers of frost started forming across its crimson skin.","Noah used that opportunity to retreat several meters away.","Then he took a stance.","Noah planted his feet firmly into a low, wide horse stance.","His muscles coiled as he adjusted his grip on the spear.","Then he began erasing every emotion within himself.","One by one, his thoughts faded.","His anger disappeared. His excitement vanished. Even his fear was erased.","Everything sank into stillness. Silence remained.","Only the spear existed. Only the path of the blade mattered.","Noah’s eyes slowly opened. There was complete calmness within them.","The atmosphere around him changed. The surrounding air grew colder as mana gathered over his blade of sword.","The young man standing there suddenly felt entirely different. He was calm. He was still. There was not a trace of emotion in his eyes.","Right now, he was emotionless. The Frost Mist finally began to disperse. The Minotaur’s vision gradually returned. Its glowing red eyes immediately locked onto Noah.","\"ROOOARRR!\"","The beast roared and charged. Its massive legs thundered against the ground.","Each step left cracks in the earth beneath it. The stone club in its hand glowed faintly with red mana.","Yet Noah didn’t react. There was no fear.","There was no hesitation. Nor there was any excitement. What remained was only focus remained.","It was as if he was standing on surface of a frozen lake still. Then he moved. His torso twisted. His muscles released all their stored power. The spearhead swept across his body in a flawless horizontal arc.","The weapon hissed through the air.","For a brief moment, the spear transformed from a piercing weapon into a sweeping scythe capable of cutting down everything before it.","Frozen Lotus Blade Art.","[Second Petal – Still Surface Cut]","SLASH!","The instant the strike completed. A distortion rippled through the air. A thin white line appeared for a fraction of a second.","Then it vanished as if never existed.","A nearly invisible blade of compressed freezing force shot forward.","Shhhhh!","The attack was impossibly fast.","The Minotaur couldn’t even perceive it.","For a moment, nothing happened.","Then a deep cut suddenly opened across its abdomen. From that cut the blood erupted outward.","A heartbeat later, frost rapidly spread from the wound. Ice crawled across the exposed flesh.","The freezing energy surged through muscles, blood vessels, and skin.","The Minotaur’s charge abruptly stopped.","\"SCCCRREEEEECHHHH!!\"","A scream of agony echoed throughout the forest. Only now did the beast realize it had been struck.","Its enormous body trembled. The stone club slipped from its grasp.","The Minotaur collapsed onto one knee.","Its glowing red eyes stared in disbelief at the frost spreading across its stomach. It didn’t notice the weapon hovering above it. High overhead floated a sword made entirely of ice.","It was silent, deadly and waiting to deliver final blow. Then it descended.","SHCKKK!!","The ice sword pierced downward with tremendous force. It tore through the thick muscles of the Minotaur’s neck. The blade penetrated deep into the back of its nape.","THUD!","The beast’s body shook violently. A final scream escaped its throat.","Then everything became silent.","The giant body crashed heavily onto the ground.","It was dead.","Noah released a long breath.","\"Fuu... that was good.\"","A satisfied smirk appeared on his face as he looked at the fallen monster.","The traces of stillness slowly disappeared from his eyes.","He walked toward the corpse.","The Minotaur looked even larger now that it lay motionless on the forest floor. Its massive horns dug into the earth.","Frost still covered portions of its wound.","\"Now I can get its mana core.\"","Noah spun his spear once before resting it on his shoulder.","\"This one has a useful core after all.\""]},{"number":179,"title":"Chapter 179: Practical Exam (4)","paragraphs":["Noah pushed the giant monster onto its back.","The Minotaur’s massive body crashed heavily against the ground, causing the surrounding earth to tremble slightly.","Its crimson skin was covered in frost, and the deep wound across its abdomen remained frozen solid.","Noah jumped onto the corpse. The mana core was usually located somewhere near the chest of monsters like this.","A dagger appeared in his hand.","\"Okay, let’s deal with it—\"","Suddenly, something shot toward him.","Noah heard it immediately.","The object tore through the air at incredible speed.","His instincts screamed. Without hesitation, he jumped to the opposite side of the Minotaur’s body.","BOOM!","A massive fireball exploded where he had been standing only a moment ago. The corpse shook from the impact.","\"Shit! I missed him!\"","An unfamiliar female voice echoed through the forest.","Noah immediately stood up and looked toward the source.","Two students emerged from between the trees. A young man and a young woman.","Noah didn’t recognize either of them. That meant they were probably from another class.","The young man carried a sword in his hand. The woman held a magic wand. Both looked ready for battle.","\"Oh? You’re Noah Eldritch, aren’t you?\" the young man asked with a grin. \"We didn’t see you properly and attacked without warning.\"","Despite his words, there wasn’t the slightest trace of apology on his face. His sword remained raised.","The girl beside him was already channeling mana through her wand.","\"No hard feelings, Noah,\" she said with a confident smile. \"This is an exam. We can’t afford to show mercy.\"","Noah simply smiled.","Then, to their confusion, he climbed back onto the Minotaur’s body before casually jumping down again.","\"Don’t worry,\" he said gently while walking toward them. \"I’m not sad or angry.\"","The distance between them slowly shortened. His smile remained calm.","\"Well then...\"","His eyes narrowed slightly.","\"Let’s end this.\"","The young woman immediately began casting. A large magic circle rapidly formed before her.","At the same time, the young man coated his sword with mana.","However Noah was faster than both of them. Mana surged through his body. Above him, ice rapidly condensed.","One weapon.","Five weapons.","Ten weapons.","Fifteen weapons.","A mixture of swords, spears, and battle axes materialized in the air. The entire process took only seconds.","Both students froze. Shock appeared on their faces.","The young woman’s concentration immediately broke. The half-formed magic circle shattered into countless particles.","Even the young man unconsciously stepped backward. \"Haha! You think this can intimidate us?\"","Noah only smiled.","He didn’t answer.","Instead all fifteen weapons shot forward simultaneously.","SHHHH!!","The air screamed.","\"Fuck!\"","The young man’s face changed dramatically. \"What are you doing? Form a barrier!\" he shouted toward his partner.","The girl hurriedly raised her wand. But she was too late.","SLASH!","Two ice swords pierced through her defenses and sliced across her side. An ice axe buried itself deep into her thigh.","\"ARGHHHH!!\"","She screamed and collapsed. At the same time, the young man immediately abandoned the fight.","He turned around and ran. Unfortunately an ice spear shot forward.","THRUST!","The weapon pierced through his back.","Noah had intentionally avoided any vital areas.","\"ARRRGHHHH!!\"","Both students fell onto the ground. Their bodies began shimmering. It was like a broken image. Like a digital glitch.","Then they disappeared completely. Teleported away by their battle gear. They would be at academy base and would be treated immediately.","So Noah didn’t need to worry about injuring them.","Noah watched them vanish.","\"They were weak.\"","He turned around and returned to the Minotaur. The battle hadn’t even lasted half a minute.","Without wasting time, he climbed onto the corpse again. Then he began cutting through its chest. \"Man, I fought one battle after another.\"","He sighed. \"Hope no new student or monster attacks me.\"","Fighting continuously had left him slightly tired. After several minutes of searching, he finally found it.","A mana core of rank E monster. A crimson crystal roughly the size of a fist.","\"Found you. This will be useful for me. \"","He wiped away the blood before placing it inside his storage ring. Afterward, Noah sat atop the Minotaur’s corpse for a while.","\"Hmm... Instructor Morgana didn’t exactly tell us the distance.\"","He clicked his tongue.","\"Dammit. We have no choice but to keep moving until we find the beacon.\"","His gaze drifted northward.","\"How far is it? What dangers are ahead? We have no idea.\"","Noah stood up.","’Also, I need to avoid Damien.’","A grim expression appeared on his face.","’That guy is crazy strong even if we both are at same core level.’","Soon, Noah resumed running north. Completely unaware that the person he wanted to avoid the most was actively searching for him.","---","Several kilometers away. A golden line suddenly appeared in the air.","A compressed projectile of radiant energy shot forward.","THRUST!","The attack pierced directly through a monster’s chest. The beast collapsed instantly.","THUD!","Behind it, three more monsters charged forward.","They resembled giant tigers covered in white fur.","Each stood over one and half meters tall. Their saber-like fangs protruded from their mouths while glowing blue eyes burned with hostility.","Damien stood calmly before them. A golden sword rested in his hand. The next moment he disappeared.","His speed resembled a flash of lightning. One moment he stood still.","The next, he had already passed all three beasts.","SLASH!","SLASH!","SLASH!","Three clean cuts appeared across their bodies. For several seconds, nothing happened. Then blood erupted into the air.","The monsters slowed. Their legs gave out beneath them.","THUD!","THUD!","THUD!","All three collapsed lifelessly. Damien flicked his sword.","Droplets of blood scattered through the air before falling onto the ground.","His expression remained disappointed. \"I haven’t met any strong students yet.\"","He sighed. \"The few I encountered were too weak.\"","What Damien didn’t know was that most students fled the moment they saw him from a distance.","Nobody wanted to fight the current Rank One student.","\"Dammit.\"","He looked toward the endless forest. \"Hope I meet some worthy opponents soon.\"","After muttering those words, Damien crouched beside the corpses and began extracting their mana cores.","Rustle.","A sound came from nearby bushes.","Damien instantly turned. His body moved before his mind even finished processing.","BOOM!","He dashed into the forest. His sword flashed.","A diagonal slash cut through the air.","CLANG!!","Steel collided against steel.","Sparks exploded.","\"Man! How did you notice me?!\"","A surprised voice rang out. Standing before Damien was a young man with green hair.","A thin rapier rested in his hand.","Damien narrowed his eyes.","\"You...\"","The two separated after the clash. \"You are Michael, aren’t you? From Class B-1?\"","Michael blinked. Then he smiled. \"Oh? It seems the famous Rank One student knows me.\"","\"Yes.\"","Damien pointed his sword at him.","\"I’ve seen you with Travis.\"","Michael laughed awkwardly.","\"Well, it’s an honor to be recognized by someone like you.\"","Then his expression turned somewhat pitiful.","\"But it seems I’m really unlucky today.\"","He raised both hands slightly.","\"How about we make a deal?\"","Damien raised an eyebrow.","\"What deal?\"","Michael immediately straightened his posture. A merchant-like smile appeared on his face. \"Simple.\"","He pointed at himself. \"You spare me.\"","Then he pointed at Damien. \"And after the exam ends, I’ll give you money.\"","Damien remained silent. Seeing no reaction, Michael hurriedly continued.","\"Or mana cores! Lots of mana cores! You can absorb them during meditation.\"","His smile widened. \"See? It’s win for both of us. You can become more stronger. don’t need to worry about money.\"","Damien stared at him. His expression remained completely blank. he couldn’t believe a young man from a noble family was actually trying to bribe him to not eliminate him.","The silence became awkward.","\"Hey.\" Michael twitched. \"Say something.\"","Damien sighed deeply. The disappointment in his eyes became obvious. \"For real?\"","He slowly raised his sword. Golden mana once again gathered around the blade.","\"You really think I’ll be moved by offers like that?\" But Damien had no plan to listen to this young master.","Michael’s smile instantly disappeared.","\"I don’t need money.\" Golden light intensified around Damien. The surrounding air trembled. His eyes sharpened. \"All I need...\"","BOOM!","The ground exploded beneath his feet. Damien shot forward. \"...is a good fight!\"","\"FUCK!\"","Michael cursed loudly and raised his rapier.","CLANG!!","Their weapons collided once again. A shockwave blasted outward. Leaves scattered across the forest as the battle officially began.","\"Fuck!\" Michael cursed as from the ground green vines dashed toward Damien’s legs.","Even on the rapier’s blade dark green colored vines with sharp thorns on it.","They also moved and grabbed Damien’s sword.","\"Argh!\" While the vines that caught his both legs also had thorns which send a sharp pain to him.","Watching him in pain made Michael smile. \"Don’t think I am weak..\" But his smile was not for much long.","Because suddenly a huge smile appeared on Damien’s face. \"Nice. I guess you are actually strong. You can give me a good fight!\"","Seeing that expression made Michael pale.","All he could do was curse. \"Fuck!\""]},{"number":180,"title":"Chapter 180: Practical Exam (5)","paragraphs":["It’s been a few hours since the race had begun.","Noah had eliminated many beasts along the way, but most of them had been low-ranked monsters. He glanced around the endless forest before muttering to himself,","\"Should I take a break?\"","His legs were beginning to feel heavy after constantly running and fighting. After a moment of thought, he shook his head.","\"No... let’s continue for another half hour. Then I’ll rest for a while.\"","Without wasting another second, he resumed his march through the dense forest.","The towering trees stretched endlessly into the sky, their enormous trunks casting long shadows over the ground. Dry leaves crunched beneath his boots while vines hung from branches like silent serpents.","As he moved, his thoughts wandered elsewhere.","’It’s the semester exam... There should be some kind of major incident... so why hasn’t anything happened yet?’","The thought refused to leave his mind.","Although Noah appeared calm on the outside, he was genuinely nervous.","He had already faced two life-threatening situations since arriving in this world. He wasn’t foolish enough to believe his luck would always hold.","After taking a slow breath, he shook those thoughts away.","’For now... I should focus on the exam.’","Rustle~","A sudden sound emerged from a nearby bush.","Noah instantly raised his left hand toward it. Mana surged through his body.","An ice sword materialized in front of his palm within a fraction of a second, its razor-sharp edge glistening beneath the scattered sunlight.","He didn’t ask who was there. He simply waited. A few seconds later, the bushes parted. A familiar figure stepped out.","\"Mary?\"","The young woman blinked in surprise.","\"Noah?\"","It was Mary.","Her short black hair swayed gently as she emerged from the bushes. She held a long wooden wand topped with an orange crystal, while traces of exhaustion were visible on her face.","With an awkward smile, she gave a small wave.","\"W-Well... hello?\"","Noah smiled back.","\"Hello.\"","The very next instant.","Whoosh!","The ice sword shot toward her at incredible speed.","Mary’s eyes widened in terror.","\"W-What?!\"","She instinctively raised her wand to cast a spell. But she was too slow.","The sword had already reached her. Her face turned pale as she tightly shut her eyes. She waited for the impact...","...","Nothing happened. After several seconds, she slowly opened one eye. The sword was hovering barely an inch away from her forehead.","Crack.","It shattered into countless sparkling ice particles before disappearing into the air.","Mary released a long breath she hadn’t realized she was holding. \"N-Noah... I thought you were going to eliminate me.\"","Noah chuckled.","\"Oh? Why would I?\"","He smiled warmly. \"You’re my friend, aren’t you?\"","Mary blinked before nodding.","\"Yes... but during the VR battle... you eliminated everyone just to reach first place.\"","\"Haha! That’s true.\"","Noah rubbed the back of his neck, laughing after remembering that battle.","’No wonder she thought I’d attack without hesitation.’","He slowly walked toward her. \"Still, I have no intention of eliminating you...\"","A mischievous smile appeared on his face. \"...unless you’ve already accumulated a huge number of points.\"","Mary immediately puffed her cheeks. \"Hey! I haven’t defeated that many monsters!\"","She crossed her arms with a helpless expression. \"I’ve mostly been running this entire time.\"","Noah raised an eyebrow.","\"Running?\"","His gaze shifted toward the direction from which she had arrived.","\"And you were running east.\"","He looked back at her. \"Why?\"","Mary lowered her head slightly, looking embarrassed. \"I... I saw Damien from afar.\"","Her voice became quieter. \"So I immediately changed direction and ran away.\"","She scratched her cheek awkwardly. \"I just wanted to get as far away from him as possible.\"","She looked at Noah. \"And... I accidentally ran into you.\"","Noah’s eyes widened. \"Wait...\"","His expression immediately became serious. \"Really?\"","Mary nodded. \"Where is he now?\"","She pointed toward the dense forest behind her. \"If you keep going in the direction I came from...\"","She thought for a moment. \"...after a few kilometers, you should find him.\" Curiosity filled her eyes. \"Do you want to fight him?\"","\"Fight?\" Noah immediately shook his head. \"No! There is absolutely no way I want to fight Damien.\"","Without another word, Noah gently grabbed Mary’s wrist. \"Come.\"","He immediately began walking in the opposite direction. \"We’ll continue this way for a while...\"","He pushed aside hanging vines and thick bushes as they moved through the forest. \"...then we’ll turn north again.\"","Mary quietly followed behind him. Her eyes slowly drifted toward the hand holding her wrist. A faint blush gradually spread across her cheeks.","She lowered her gaze. Then she looked up again. Her eyes rested on Noah’s broad back as he walked ahead, carefully clearing the path for both of them.","For some reason... Her heartbeat became slightly faster. A few moments later, Noah seemed to realize something.","He immediately released her wrist. Turning his head slightly, he smiled apologetically.","\"Sorry. I grabbed your wrist without thinking.\"","He gestured beside him. \"Walk next to me.\"","Mary glanced at her now-empty hand. For just a brief moment, a tiny feeling of disappointment flashed across her face. So small that even she failed to notice it.","She quietly moved beside him. After walking in silence for a while, Noah spoke again.","\"So...\"","He glanced sideways at her.","\"Are you aiming for the Top 100? Or maybe something higher?\"","Mary smiled sheepishly. \"No.\"","She shook her head. \"Top 100 is already good enough for me.\"","\"That’s a realistic goal.\" Noah nodded. \"But you should aim higher.\"","A confident smile spread across his face. \"I want to finish in the Top 10.\"","Mary looked at him before smiling warmly.","\"Haha... I know you can do it, Noah.\"","She spoke with complete sincerity. \"You scored so many points during the first unit exam. And if you also reach the finish line within the Top 10...\"","She smiled brightly. \"...I’m sure your overall first-year ranking will rise by a lot.\"","\"I’m hoping for that too.\"","The two of them continued walking together through the vast forest.","The only sounds accompanying them were the rustling leaves beneath their feet and the distant cries of monsters echoing from somewhere deep within the wilderness.","---","Several kilometers away from Noah and Mary...","The forest became even denser.","The towering trees blocked almost all sunlight, leaving the surroundings dim despite it still being daytime.","The ground was covered in thick grass, tangled roots, and countless creeping vines that spread like an endless green carpet.","At first glance, nothing seemed unusual.","However...","Hidden beneath the overgrown vegetation was a narrow passage.","The entrance was so perfectly concealed by vines and moss that even someone standing only a few meters away would never notice it.","The small passage descended deep beneath the earth.","Into the darkness below.","Deep within the hidden passage stretched a massive underground corridor.","At the end of it stood an enormous iron door.","It was pitch black, ancient, and weathered by countless years. Strange symbols were engraved across its surface, while rust covered parts of the thick metal. Despite its age, the door radiated an eerie sense of majesty.","More importantly... It was slightly open. Someone had already entered.","\"Man... this is terrible.\" A dark-haired man with a short beard let out a frustrated sigh as he ran a hand through his hair.","\"Yeah... I know.\" His companion, a man with dark burgundy hair, replied with an equally troubled expression.","Both men appeared to be in their late twenties, perhaps around thirty years old.","\"How can our timing be this bad?\" the bearded man complained. \"We finally decided to come to this forest, and just a few days later Novaris Academy came to inspect this forest then today brought hundreds of students here for their examination.\"","The burgundy-haired man could only shake his head. \"Our luck is really terrible.\"","He glanced toward the enormous iron door before continuing, \"But after searching for so many days, we finally managed to find this place.\"","The bearded man nodded. \"Now we can only hope that none of those academy students discovers these ruins.\"","\"They shouldn’t.\" The burgundy-haired man touched the necklace hidden beneath his clothes.","\"Also we’ve been able to hide our presence this whole time because of the Null Amulet.\"","A faint smile appeared on the bearded man’s face.","\"Yeah. We originally bought it to avoid attracting monsters.\"","He chuckled.","\"But I never imagined it would be this effective. It definitely saved us from a lot of unnecessary trouble.\"","The burgundy-haired man looked back toward the ancient doorway. \"Well...\"","His eyes shone with anticipation. \"Let’s go inside. I’m excited to see what these ruins actually hold.\"","A grin spread across his face. \"The boss will definitely be pleased once he learns that we found this place.\"","\"True.\"","The two men exchanged a nod before walking through the massive iron doorway.","Beyond it lay a structure unlike anything they had expected.","The floor beneath their feet was paved with perfectly cut stone slabs that had somehow remained intact despite the passage of countless centuries.","The walls were crafted from polished stone and adorned with intricate carvings depicting forgotten civilizations, mysterious symbols, and majestic creatures whose identities had long been lost to history.","\"It’s... beautiful, honestly.\"","The bearded man couldn’t help but admire the architecture. Neither of them had expected such a magnificent structure to remain hidden beneath the forest.","As they continued deeper, another passage came into view. This one sloped downward. A long flight of ancient stone stairs disappeared into the darkness below.","The two men exchanged another glance. Without hesitation... They began descending the staircase. Completely unaware of what awaited them beneath the ancient ruins."]},{"number":181,"title":"Chapter 181: Unknown Ruin","paragraphs":["\"Albert, what did the boss tell you about this ruin?\" the burgundy-haired man asked the bearded man beside him, whose name was Albert.","Albert shrugged lightly. \"She didn’t tell me much. But she did say this is a temple dedicated to some god.\"","Boris raised an eyebrow. \"Hmm... now that’s interesting. You never told me that before. I mean, we’ve been searching for this place for so many days.\"","Albert glanced at him. \"Well, you never asked.\"","\"Tch!\"","After a brief silence, Albert looked toward Boris. \"By the way, Boris. Did you send our location?\"","Boris nodded. \"Yes. I already did that.\"","\"Good.\" Albert replied with a nod.","The two men continued descending the ancient stone staircase. Each of them carried a burning torch, its flickering flame casting dancing shadows across the damp walls while illuminating the darkness ahead.","The deeper they went, the colder the air became. Finally, they reached the bottom. Before them stretched a massive underground hall.","Towering stone pillars stood in perfect rows on both sides, forming a long path that disappeared into the darkness ahead.","Each pillar was covered with intricate carvings and ancient patterns that had somehow survived the passage of countless years.","The craftsmanship was astonishing.","Albert slowly looked around with amazement.","\"Wow... this place really is incredible. Despite being buried underground for so many years, it still looks this well-preserved.\"","Boris slowly scanned the surroundings with his torch. \"Yes... but this place gives me chills.\" he admitted quietly.","The two cautiously walked farther into the hall. They examined the walls, pillars, and carvings as they advanced, trying to find anything unusual.","Soon, their eyes landed on an enormous stone door standing at the end of the hall. Both of them walked toward it.","Albert looked at the gigantic entrance with curiosity. \"Will this lead us to another chamber?\" he wondered aloud.","Boris scratched his beard thoughtfully.","\"Maybe.\"","He stepped forward and planted both hands against the heavy stone door. With a deep breath, he pushed with all his strength.","Nothing happened. The gigantic door didn’t move even the slightest bit.","Seeing Boris fail, Albert immediately stepped beside him.","\"Move over.\"","The two men pushed together. Their muscles tensed. Veins bulged across their arms as they poured more strength into it.","Still... The door remained completely motionless.","Not willing to give up, they circulated mana through their bodies to increase their physical strength. Once again, they pushed.","Nothing happened. Then they tried pulling it.","Again nothing happened.","They even attempted to slide it sideways. Yet no matter what they did, the ancient door refused to budge.","Albert finally stepped back and let out a tired sigh.","\"I think I know why it didn’t budge at all.\"","Boris turned toward him.","\"Why?\"","Albert pointed toward the massive stone door.","\"This must have originally been the entrance to the temple. Since we’re underground now, the other side is probably buried beneath tons of soil. Of course it won’t open.\"","Boris blinked for a moment before nodding in realization.","\"Oh... you’re right.\"","Albert dusted off his hands.","\"Let’s go to the other side of the hall. We might find another door.\"","\"Agreed.\"","The two men turned around and walked toward the opposite end of the enormous chamber.","As they had expected. There was indeed another stone door.","It was just as massive as the first one. However...Unlike the previous entrance...","This one was slightly open. Both men exchanged cautious glances.","Without saying another word, they slowly approached it.","Albert placed both hands against the heavy stone door. Boris did the same.","Together, they pushed.","GRRRRRR...","The enormous stone door slowly slid open with a deep grinding sound that echoed throughout the silent temple.","A gust of ancient, stale air escaped from within. The two men instinctively tightened their grips on their torches before carefully stepping inside.","The chamber beyond was another vast hall. The torchlight swept across the darkness as they cautiously examined every corner.","At first... They found nothing.","The room appeared completely empty.","Then their torchlight fell upon something standing at the very center of the chamber.","Both men froze. Their eyes widened.","Towering before them was a gigantic statue.","Albert’s voice trembled. \"Th-that’s... the god...\"","---","It was getting late in the evening.","SCREEECHHH!!","A spider-type monster let out a shrill, agonizing scream before its enormous body collapsed onto the forest floor.","BOOM!","Dust rose into the air as the monster twitched a few times before becoming completely still.","Noah let out a long breath and casually ran a hand through his silver-white hair, fixing the strands that had become messy during the battle.","\"Fuu... We’ve killed quite a lot of monsters along the way.\" he said with a satisfied smile.","Mary looked at him before lowering her gaze.","Her hands were still tightly gripping her wand. \"Yes... but you killed most of them.\" she said softly.","Her eyes drifted toward the pile of monster corpses scattered around them.","After a brief pause, she continued in a guilty tone. \"And you helped me kill so many as well... Honestly, you deserved those kills yourself.\"","Her shoulders drooped as she looked down at the ground with a dejected expression.","Noah watched her quietly. He tried his best not to think she looked cute.","Unfortunately...He failed. Even when she was feeling guilty, she somehow managed to look adorable.","A faint smile appeared on his face. He walked over to her and gently placed his hand on her head.","Slowly stroking her soft hair, he spoke reassuringly.","\"Don’t worry, girl. If I really wanted those kills, I would’ve simply stolen them myself.\"","Mary’s cheeks instantly turned red.","She quickly stepped away from him while covering her head.","\"H-Hey! Don’t do that!! You’re always like this! Hmph!\" she protested with an embarrassed pout as she looked away.","Noah couldn’t help but chuckle. With a teasing smile, he tilted his head.","\"Always like what? Care to elaborate?\"","Mary looked back at him nervously. Although embarrassed, she still gathered enough courage to speak her mind.","\"Y-You... You know... You’re always saying sweet things to girls...\"","She hesitated before asking, \"Do you know what people like that are called?\"","Noah folded his arms and smiled. \"What? Please tell me.\"","Mary pointed at him with a trembling finger. \"Y-You’re a playboy... Y-You’re a womanizer... A-And you’re... you’re a simp!!\""]},{"number":182,"title":"Chapter 182: Search For Kaelan","paragraphs":["The smile on Noah’s face immediately disappeared.","He frowned. \"What did you just say?\" he asked in a cold voice.","The sudden change in his tone startled Mary.","She instinctively took a step back. \"I-I mean... exactly what you heard.\"","Noah simply shook his head.","\"Sigh...\"","He let out a tired sigh before rubbing his forehead. \"Even you misunderstand me...\"","He looked straight into her eyes. \"I’m none of those three.\"","Mary crossed her arms. \"Then what are you?\"","Noah placed a hand on his chest and proudly declared with a completely serious face,","\"I am a real gentleman. Who talk nice to all girls.\"","Mary immediately snorted. \"Hmph! No one will believe your lies.\"","Noah’s lips twitched. He stared at her for a moment before speaking again.","\"Alright... You called me a playboy—I was fine with that.\"","He raised one finger. \"You called me a womanizer—I was still fine with that.\"","Then he pointed at her dramatically. \"But a simp? Damn it! Let me show you that I am definitely not a simp.\"","Mary’s eyes widened. A bad feeling suddenly rose within her. \"W-Wait! Noah!\"","But she was too late.","Noah suddenly dashed toward her.","Before she could react. He wrapped one arm around her waist.","\"W-Wait!! What are you doing?!\"","In one smooth motion, he lifted her into a princess carry.","Mary’s face instantly turned bright red. \"W-Wait! Put me down!!\"","Noah ignored every single word.","Instead... He began spinning around in circles while carrying her.","\"Ahhh!!\"","Mary instinctively wrapped both arms around his neck so she wouldn’t fall. The world spun around her.","After several rounds, Noah finally slowed down. He carefully lowered her toward the ground.","Mary let out a relieved sigh.","Finally... He was putting her down. But not on her feet.","He put her as he had lifted her, her rear touched against the surface. Her eyes widened. Something incredibly cold touched her rear.","She quickly looked down. The ground beneath her had completely transformed into a smooth sheet of ice.","\"Kyaaahhh!! It’s cold! It’s so cold!\"","Panicking, she immediately tried to stand properly.","Slip!","Her feet slid across the icy surface.","She completely lost her balance.","\"Ahhh!!\"","She struggled desperately, trying to stand up again. Only to slip once more.","Meanwhile...A short distance away.","Noah leaned casually against a nearby tree with his arms folded across his chest. A smug smile rested on his face as he quietly enjoyed watching her struggle.","\"Noah!! Help! It’s cold!!\"","Mary cried out with teary eyes.","\"I’m sorry! I was only teasing you! Noah!!\"","Her watery eyes pleaded for mercy.","Noah watched her silently.","Honestly... If Ophelia or Emma had been in Mary’s place... He would’ve enjoyed the scene much longer. He probably wouldn’t have helped them at all.","But... Mary was different. In the end, Noah sighed.","He raised one finger.","Snap!","With a simple flick of his finger.","Crack!","The ice shattered into countless pieces before instantly melting away.","Mary hurriedly stood up and dusted herself off. She looked both exhausted and embarrassed.","Noah smiled faintly. \"Hope you won’t call me by those titles again.\"","Mary nodded so quickly that it almost looked comical. \"Yes!! You’re not like that!\"","A victorious smirk spread across Noah’s face.","Rustle","His expression suddenly changed. The smile disappeared. His brows furrowed. Slowly, he turned his head toward the forest on his right.","There was silence. Nothing was there.","’What?’","’I could’ve sworn someone was watching me...’","’But there’s no one.’","Mary noticed his reaction and immediately became serious as well.","She tightened her grip around her wand and looked in the same direction.","\"Was there someone?\" she asked cautiously.","Noah remained silent for a few moments as he carefully observed the dense forest.","Finally, he spoke.","\"Hmm... I felt like someone was watching us...\"","He narrowed his eyes.","\"...But I guess I was wrong.\"","Mary looked around once more.","\"Really?\"","Noah stayed quiet for another moment before making his decision.","He nodded.","\"Let’s go in that direction.\"","Mary blinked.","\"Why?\"","\"There’s a possibility another student was watching us.\" Noah replied calmly.","\"Let’s go.\"","Mary nodded without hesitation.","\"Okay. Let’s go.\"","The two of them immediately broke into a run, heading toward the exact direction where Noah had sensed someone watching them.","----","Meanwhile, farther ahead of Noah and Mary, a lone figure wearing a hood raced silently through the forest.","His footsteps were swift and light, barely making a sound as he weaved between the towering trees.","Just a few minutes ago...","He had been the one secretly watching Noah and Mary from a distance.","However he had absolutely nothing to do with them. As he continued running at full speed, the hood covering his head gradually slipped backward.","His face was finally revealed. Two black horns rose proudly from his head. His skin was dark and tanned.","He was none other than... A demon. The demon gritted his teeth in frustration while scanning the forest ahead.","\"Dammit! Where is he?\" he muttered under his breath.","His expression darkened further. \"We’re still unable to find him. We need to hurry before we’re discovered by the academy staff.\"","BEEP! BEEP!","A notification echoed from inside his cloak. Without slowing down, he reached into his pocket and pulled out a sleek black communication device.","The screen lit up.","He immediately accepted the call while continuing to sprint through the forest. A voice came from the other side.","\"Did you find Kaelan Nightfall?\"","The demon shook his head while leaping over a fallen tree. \"No, I haven’t.\"","A frustrated sigh came from the communicator.","\"Dammit...\"","After a brief pause, the voice asked,","\"Where are you currently?\"","The demon glanced around while maintaining his speed.","\"On the eastern side of the forest.\"","\"Hah...\" The man on the other end let out a tired sigh.","\"Should we regroup? It’s going to be night soon.\"","The demon nodded.","\"Sure. I’ll share my coordinates with you and the others. Let’s meet there.\"","\"Also...\" the voice continued seriously,","\"Keep an eye on your surroundings and the sky. The academy is monitoring the students using drones.\"","The demon’s expression remained calm.","\"Yes. I’m aware. Don’t worry.\"","\"—\"","The call ended. The communication device’s screen turned black. The demon slipped it back into his pocket without stopping for even a second.","He continued racing through the forest. His destination remained unknown.","His only objective. To find a student named Kaelan Nightfall.","But, What exactly did he want from Kaelan? Had he come here merely to find him... Or had he come here to kill him?","Meanwhile, far away from the forest... Deep beneath the earth.","Two unknown men continued exploring an ancient underground temple, searching its mysterious halls for answers hidden within the forgotten ruins.","And while all of this was happening.","Noah remained completely unaware of everything unfolding around him."]},{"number":183,"title":"Chapter 183: Kaelan Vs Demon (1)","paragraphs":["Stomp.","Stomp.","The sound of footsteps echoed through the forest, blending with the gentle breeze and the rustling leaves of the towering trees.","A young man with black hair and gray eyes walked cautiously. His sharp gaze constantly swept his surroundings, searching for any sign of monsters or other students.","He was none other than Kaelan. A pair of daggers were gripped tightly in his hands.","\"It’s getting late... I’ve come a long way. I’ll take a rest after a while.\"","As he continued walking, his thoughts drifted toward Damien.","He wanted to fight him... If possible, he wanted to fight right now.","It didn’t matter if he lost. It didn’t matter if he failed to reach the finish line.","He simply wanted a fair battle against Damien.","\"Then there’s Noah.\"","Kaelan already knew that Noah had become incredibly strong compared to how he had been at the beginning of the academy.","\"He’s definitely at the High Awakened Core Rank.\"","He muttered quietly. \"But I also reached that level two days ago...\"","A determined look appeared in his eyes.","\"After Damien... I’ll fight him.\"","Rustle~","Whoosh!","Something shot toward him at incredible speed.","\"What?!\"","Kaelan instinctively raised his twin daggers and crossed them.","Clang!","A sword crashed into his daggers.","The impact was so overwhelming that Kaelan was blasted backward. His body was thrown through the air before he slid across the ground, leaving a long trail in the dirt.","He immediately forced himself back onto his feet.","Standing before him was a man. He appeared to be around thirty years old. But what surprised Kaelan the most wasn’t his age...","It was his appearance. The man standing before him was a Demon.","\"Lucky me...\"","The demon smiled coldly. \"To find you here. The timing couldn’t have been more perfect.\"","Kaelan tightened his grip on his daggers.","His mind instantly recalled the battle against the demon Marbas...","The battle where several students had lost their lives.","Darkness slowly began covering both dagger blades. Black smoky trails leaked from them and drifted through the air.","Mana surged out from his core and flowed into his arms and legs, strengthening every muscle.","\"You want to fight?\"","The demon asked coldly. Kaelan answered only with a calm gaze.The next instant.","He vanished from his position.","Clang!","His daggers collided against the demon’s sword.","Clang! Clang!","Kaelan quickly retreated several meters before slashing both daggers outward.","Two razor-sharp crescents made entirely of darkness flew forward in an X-shaped pattern.","The demon’s sword glowed with a gray aura.","He casually swung it.","BOOM!","The collision produced a small explosion. The blast sent dust and fallen leaves flying in every direction.","Kaelan narrowed his eyes.","’He’s strong.’","Much stronger than any monster he had encountered so far.","The demon lowered his sword, his crimson eyes studying the young man with faint interest.","\"Not bad.\"","His deep voice echoed through the forest.","\"A first-year student capable of releasing such power.\"","He slowly pointed his blade toward Kaelan.","\"But that’s all.\"","Boom!","The ground beneath the demon suddenly shattered.","He disappeared.","\"So fast—!\"","Kaelan barely reacted in time.","Clang!","His crossed daggers intercepted the descending blade.","The tremendous force bent his knees.","Crack!","The earth beneath his feet fractured into a spiderweb of cracks.","\"Ghk!\"","Kaelan gritted his teeth.","The demon wasn’t simply physically stronger...","His sword felt unbelievably heavy.","It was gravity magic.","Before Kaelan could recover.","Bang!","The demon drove a kick straight into his abdomen.","\"Cough!\"","Kaelan was blasted backward, crashing through several bushes before rolling across the ground.","He immediately flipped back onto his feet. Blood trickled from the corner of his mouth. The demon casually walked toward him.","\"You’ve got decent instincts.\"","He slowly raised his sword.","\"But instincts alone won’t save you.\"","Dark mana surged around Kaelan.","The black smoke surrounding his twin daggers thickened.","His gray eyes became completely calm. His body lowered.","[First Fang]","Whoosh!","His figure split into several black afterimages. The demon’s eyes narrowed slightly. Three Kaelans attacked simultaneously from different directions.","Slash!","Slash!","Slash!","The demon calmly swung his sword once.","A gray ripple spread outward.","Boom!","The immense pressure instantly dispersed every illusion.","Only the real Kaelan remained.","The demon effortlessly blocked both daggers.","Clang!","Clang!","Kaelan twisted his body. His right dagger stabbed toward the demon’s ribs while the left slashed toward his neck.","His attacks flowed like dancing shadows.","He was fast, precise and deadly.","The demon simply stepped backward. Every strike missed by mere centimeters.","\"You are too predictable.\"","The demon’s free hand suddenly grabbed Kaelan’s wrist.","\"What—\"","Boom!","Kaelan was slammed directly into the ground. The impact blasted apart the surrounding earth.","Dust rose everywhere.","\"Cough!\"","Kaelan spat another mouthful of blood.","The demon didn’t stop. His sword glowed with gray mana. Several magic circles appeared around him.","[Gravity Spear]","The magic circles trembled.","The next instant...","Dozens of compressed gray spears shot toward Kaelan.","Without hesitation, Kaelan activated his Innate Ability.","[Black Star]","The surrounding mana trembled.","The incoming gravity spears visibly weakened the moment they entered the sphere surrounding him.","Threads of mana were forcefully drawn away from them.","Even the loose mana lingering throughout the air began flowing toward Kaelan.","The gravity spears became slightly smaller. Their speed decreased.","But only slightly.","Boom!","Boom!","Boom!","The remaining spears exploded around him. Each spear created a small gravitational field upon impact.","Kaelan darted through the barrage, narrowly avoiding the attacks.","Even so, his body grew increasingly heavier as the surrounding gravity continuously pulled at him.","Several spears still grazed his shoulder and thigh, leaving bloody wounds.","The weapons themselves were composed of compressed gravitational energy.","Kaelan breathed heavily.","’I can’t absorb too much... They’re simply too powerful.’","The demon observed everything with mild curiosity.","\"So that’s your Innate Ability. A mana absorption type. Interesting.\"","The demon got some idea about his ability. What it does.","Which gave him more advantages. But Kaelan was not going to give up that fast.","There was another way to be safe, self harm and get eliminated.","So it was not like Kaelan had no chance of surviving."]},{"number":184,"title":"Chapter 184: Kaelan Vs Demon (2)","paragraphs":["Kaelan ignored him. He extended one of his daggers. Darkness gathered around its blade.","[Second Fang]","[Night Pursuit]","He poured an enormous amount of mana into the technique.","Countless black serpents, each several meters long, erupted from the ground.","They rushed toward the demon from every direction.","The demon remained expressionless.","\"Hmph.\"","He slowly raised one hand.","A massive gray magic circle appeared beneath his feet.","[Gravity Field]","Boom!","The surrounding space suddenly became unbearably heavy.","The darkness collapsed unnaturally.","The grass flattened instantly.","Even the nearby trees groaned beneath the overwhelming pressure.","Kaelan’s concentration was disrupted.","His body abruptly sank.","\"Ghh...!\"","His knees nearly touched the ground. Every muscle screamed in agony. It felt as though an invisible mountain had been placed upon his shoulders.","Even lifting his daggers became difficult.","The demon slowly approached.","Each step felt impossibly heavy.","Crunch.","Crunch.","Crunch.","\"You’re a talented young man.\"","His cold voice echoed throughout the forest.","\"No wonder they want you dead.\"","\"But...\"","\"You’re still far too inexperienced.\"","Kaelan gritted his teeth.","His muscles bulged as he forced himself back upright.","Black mana erupted around him once again.","Then a massive Black Star formed behind him and rapidly expanded.","This time, he used his Innate Ability far more aggressively.","Normally, he created the Black Star inside his body to absorb mana.","But now he manifested it outside himself on a much larger scale.","Its attractive force increased dramatically.","Loose mana from the Gravity Field began rushing toward him. The overwhelming pressure weakened but only slightly.","Veins bulged across Kaelan’s arms.","Blood seeped from the corner of his mouth. His muscles trembled violently. The strain was becoming unbearable.","’Damn it...I’m reaching my limit!’","The demon noticed immediately.","\"Overusing your ability?\"","A cruel smile spread across his face.","\"Then let me finish this.\"","Gray mana exploded from his body.","The entire forest trembled.","Leaves, stones, broken branches, and debris rose into the air under the terrifying pull of gravity.","The demon slowly raised his sword.","Dense gray mana coated the blade. Gradually the mana condensed into a solid, razor-sharp edge surrounding the weapon.","It gleamed with an eerie gray radiance.","An overwhelming amount of mana erupted from his body. The surrounding space distorted. Even the air itself seemed to grow heavier.","Kaelan’s instincts screamed at him.","This attack...","’If it lands...I’ll die instantly I won’t even be able to teleport back to the base.’","Sweat rolled down his forehead as he tightened his grip on his twin daggers.","Despite knowing the enormous gap between them.","He still refused to lower his weapons.","Mana surged around Kaelan’s twin daggers as black darkness wrapped tightly around both blades.","He was ready to harm himself before that attack would kill him. So he could teleport back to the base.","\"Now... die!\" the demon roared.","But before the demon could swing his sword.","Whoosh! Whoosh! Whoosh!","Multiple ice weapons shot toward him at tremendous speed.","The demon sensed the incoming danger instantly. He immediately changed directions and swung his sword horizontally.","A slash formed from compressed gravitational energy tore through the air.","Crack!","Boom!","Every ice weapon was sliced apart and shattered upon contact.","The slash continued forward with terrifying force, cleanly cutting through several massive ancient trees behind them.","Crack!","BOOM!!","The towering trees began crashing to the ground.","At the very same moment, something erupted from beneath the ground where the demon had been standing.","His instincts screamed at him.","Without even having time to reinforce himself with mana, he leaped into the air.","Sharp, gigantic spikes of ice burst from the earth, piercing toward the sky where he had stood only an instant earlier.","At the same time, a massive sphere of blazing fire shot out from the forest and rushed toward the demon.","\"What the hell?!\" the demon shouted in shock as he twisted his body to face the incoming fireball.","Stomp!","Stomp!","Stomp!","Rapid footsteps echoed through the forest.","Someone sprinted from behind the demon.","Emerging from behind a giant tree was Noah.","At that moment, he was holding a sword.","Its blade was coated in beautiful, crystal-blue ice that shimmered beneath the fading evening light.","Without wasting a second, Noah swung the sword in a smooth horizontal arc.","Slash!","A razor-thin compressed slash of freezing frost silently shot through the air.","\"Fuck!\"","Kaelan refused to let the opportunity slip away.","He immediately conjured another spell.","Several dark projectiles condensed from pure darkness and blasted toward the demon.","Everything happened far too quickly.","The demon had almost no time to react.","\"Shit!!\"","He bent one knee as a gray magic circle appeared beneath his feet.","The gravity around his body instantly lessened.","Using the reduced weight to his advantage, he launched himself high into the sky.","BOOM!!!","The three attacks collided exactly where the demon had been standing only moments earlier.","A tremendous explosion erupted, sending violent shockwaves in every direction.","But Noah had prepared much more than that.","Dozens of ice weapons were still floating high above the battlefield.","The sword vanished from Noah’s right hand as his spear instantly appeared in its place.","He extended his left hand forward.","\"Arrghhh!!\"","The moment Noah saw the demon leap into the air, he commanded three ice swords and two ice spears to close the distance and wound him. If not kill him outright. At the same time he started to conjured a new spell.","The demon swung his sword desperately.","Slash!","Slash!","He managed to destroy two of the incoming swords.","Thud!","One ice sword pierced straight through his thigh.","Another ice spear tore across his cheek, leaving behind a deep, bloody cut.","The final spear slashed across his right arm, carving a long wound through the flesh.","Blood splattered through the air.","Seeing the demon beginning to fall back toward the ground, Noah immediately shouted,","\"Kaelan! Myra! Prepare your attacks! Don’t give this demon any chance or time to recover!\"","Mana rapidly poured out of Noah’s body as a large blue ice magic circle formed on the ground exactly where the demon was about to land.","For the past few months, Noah had focused almost entirely on mastering weapon arts...","But he had still learned one new spell.","Now was the perfect moment to use it.","His Adaptive Learning not only allowed him to learn techniques faster, but also enabled him to adapt continuously during battle.","Because of that, his combat growth far exceeded that of ordinary people.","The magic circle flashed brilliantly.","A violent storm of freezing winds and razor-sharp ice shards erupted across the area where the demon landed.","\"ARGHHHH!!\"","The demon was instantly caught inside the raging blizzard as he fell down.","Using his gravity affinity, he attempted to suppress the storm and calm the raging winds.","But before he could break free, three blazing fire lances shot directly toward him. They had been cast by Myra, who had finally emerged from the forest.","At the same time, Kaelan crossed his twin daggers.","Slash!","Two crescent-shaped blades of darkness formed an X as they shot toward the trapped demon.","This time every attack struck perfectly.","BOOOOM!!!","---","[A/N: Well I was thinking of writing small fight...but then thought I didn’t show much powers of Kaelan.. so went into detail. Sorry guys!!]"]},{"number":185,"title":"Chapter 185: More Demons","paragraphs":["BOOM!","Smoke and dust billowed in every direction.","Thud!","A body crashed heavily onto the ground. It was the demon. He was dead.","’Good... he didn’t use any defensive magic.’","Noah let out a tired breath. His mana had been drained considerably during the battle.","Without wasting any time, he reached into his storage ring, pulled out a mana recovery potion, and drank it in one gulp.","Meanwhile, Mary hurried over to Kaelan and immediately began treating his injuries with healing magic.","Fortunately, his wounds were only minor.","’That demon wasn’t overwhelmingly stronger... only one rank above us.’","Noah walked toward the demon’s corpse.","Its body was covered in horrific injuries. Some areas had been burned black by flames, others were frozen solid beneath thick layers of ice, while countless deep cuts covered its flesh. Blood continued to seep from the wounds, staining the forest floor crimson.","He crouched beside the corpse and searched it thoroughly.","Unfortunately, he found nothing of value.","The only thing he recovered was a black communication device.","However, it had already been destroyed during the battle.","Clicking his tongue, Noah stood up and walked back toward Kaelan.","Kaelan remained seated on the ground while Myra continued healing him.","Noah stopped before them.","\"Why is a demon here...? Anyway, are you alright?\"","Kaelan nodded lightly.","\"Yes... I’m fine.\"","He paused before continuing.","\"Also... that demon looked like he was searching specifically for me.\"","\"He wanted to kill me.\"","Noah frowned.","\"Searching for you?\"","\"Now that’s strange.\"","He folded his arms while thinking.","\"Why would they do that? Does your family have some sort of conflict with a demon family?\"","Kaelan rolled his eyes.","\"Don’t talk nonsense.\"","\"Our race has never been on good terms with demons.\"","\"But the fact that they specifically targeted me...\"","\"...that’s what’s strange.\"","Noah nodded thoughtfully.","\"True.\"","\"It would make sense if they were trying to kill as many Academy students as possible to send a message.\"","\"But targeting only you...\"","\"...that feels different.\"","A worried expression appeared on Myra’s face.","\"But what should we do now?\"","\"There might be more demons in this forest.\"","\"And we don’t have any way to contact the instructors.\"","Noah nodded before answering calmly.","\"Well...\"","\"We’ll simply injure ourselves enough to get eliminated.\"","\"Once we’re teleported back to the base, we can immediately report everything.\"","Kaelan looked between Noah and Myra.","\"So... should I eliminate myself now?\"","Noah answered without hesitation.","\"Of course. You’re the one they’re after. You should be the first to leave.\"","Kaelan remained silent for a long moment. His gray eyes stayed fixed on the ground as countless thoughts raced through his mind.","Before entering this examination. He had wanted to perform well. He had wanted to fight Damien.","He had wanted to challenge Noah. He had wanted to prove his strength and finish among the top-ranked students.","But now everything had changed.","He slowly let out a long sigh.","\"I guess...I have no choice.\"","His voice carried obvious disappointment.","\"I’ll eliminate myself.\"","He clenched his fists before slowly relaxing them again.","\"This exam no longer matters.\"","Noah nodded. \"That’s the smartest decision.\"","Then, after thinking for a moment, he suddenly spoke again.","\"...On second thought.\"","Both Kaelan and Mary turned to look at him.","\"Let’s all eliminate ourselves.\"","His gaze shifted toward the dense forest surrounding them.","\"Now that we know demons have infiltrated the examination grounds, the Academy will most likely stop the exam.\"","\"So there’s no point in continuing.\"","Kaelan thought about it for several seconds before nodding.","\"...You’re right.\"","Myra, who had remained silent until now, also nodded.","\"Yes. The instructors need to know immediately.\"","The trio had just made their decision.","BOOM!!","A deafening explosion suddenly echoed through the forest.","The ground trembled violently beneath their feet.","All three instantly raised their weapons as their eyes snapped toward the source of the explosion.","Something was coming.","Crash!!","A figure burst through several massive trees before being hurled straight toward them.","\"So fast!\"","Noah instinctively leaped aside.","The flying body slammed directly into Kaelan.","BOOM!!","The two of them rolled across the forest floor before finally coming to a stop.","Noah immediately looked toward the person who had been thrown.","His eyes widened.","\"Damien!\"","Damien quickly pushed himself off Kaelan and got back to his feet.","His Academy-issued battle gear was torn in several places.","Cuts covered both of his arms, while blood slowly trickled down one side of his forehead.","His breathing was noticeably heavier than usual.","Without wasting a second, he looked at everyone and spoke in a grave voice.","\"Demons...\"","He tightened his grip around his sword.","\"Demons are here.\"","At that moment, three cloaked figures slowly emerged from between the towering trees.","Their movements were calm and unhurried, as though they had already secured victory.","The atmosphere instantly turned heavy.","Every student assumed a fighting stance.","Noah lowered his center of gravity and firmly gripped his spear.","Kaelan stepped forward despite his injuries, drawing both daggers.","Mary raised her wand as mana gathered around the crystal fixed at its tip.","The figure standing in the center slowly lowered his hood.","Two black horns curved upward from his forehead.","His crimson eyes swept across the students with cold indifference.","He was a demon.","The two figures beside him also removed their hoods, revealing themselves to be demons as well.","The leading demon took a slow step forward. He was holding a spear. His icy gaze settled directly on Kaelan.","\"Good.\"","A faint smile appeared on his face.","\"We found Kaelan.\"","He glanced toward the two demons behind him.","\"Xavier... Daniel...Prepare it.\"","The moment those words left his mouth, Xavier and Daniel immediately began forming rapid hand seals.","Their fingers moved with incredible speed. Dark crimson mana poured from their bodies. The surrounding air suddenly grew heavy.","A gigantic magic array slowly spread beneath their feet, its countless ancient runes illuminating the forest floor with an ominous crimson glow.","The formation expanded continuously, covering dozens of meters.","Its strange symbols pulsed rhythmically, radiating an unsettling aura that instinctively put everyone on guard.","Noah narrowed his eyes.","\"...What are they trying to do?\"","The crimson magic array continued spreading across the forest floor.","Ancient runes connected with one another, forming an intricate pattern that stretched throughout the battlefield.","Noah’s expression became increasingly serious.","\"...What is that?\"","The leading demon smiled coldly.","\"You Academy students rely far too much on your precious battle suits.\"","He slowly raised one hand.","\"Did you really think we would come here without preparing for them?\"","The crimson array suddenly flared.","Hummmmmm!","A strange vibration spread throughout the surrounding forest.","The communication device attached to Noah’s battle suit suddenly emitted a sharp warning tone.","[WARNING!]","[Emergency System Interference Detected.]","[Spatial Anchor Locked.]","[Automatic Emergency Teleportation Offline.]","Noah’s pupils contracted.","\"What?!\"","The warning wasn’t limited to him.","The same crimson message appeared on every student’s wrist display.","Kaelan immediately checked his own interface.","\"...The emergency teleport...\"","\"...It’s disabled.\"","Myra’s face turned pale.","\"That’s impossible...\"","The leading demon chuckled.","\"It was impossible.\"","\"But this little toy...\"","He pulled out a dark crimson rectangular device covered in ancient runes.","\"...was specially prepared for Novaris Academy.\"","\"This array amplifies its power.\"","\"As long as you remain inside this barrier, every spatial transmission linked to your battle suits will be jammed.\"","\"The suits can still monitor your health.\"","\"They can still record your points.\"","\"But they can no longer establish a spatial lock.\"","\"They cannot teleport you.\"","After explaining, the demon calmly returned the device to his cloak.","\"The only way out now is to kill us or die.\"","Silence descended upon the battlefield.","For the first time since the examination had begun...","The students realized they were no longer protected by the Academy."]},{"number":186,"title":"Chapter 186: Battle","paragraphs":["The demon standing in the center had dark gray skin, but apart from that, his appearance was almost identical to a human’s.","Two black horns curved upward from his forehead, and his crimson eyes carried a cold, emotionless gaze.","A spear held in his right hand. A faint smile appeared on his face.","\"Hello there...\" he said calmly. \"My name is Botis.\"","Damien tightened his grip around his sword. \"Where is Ken?\"","Noah glanced at him in surprise. \"Ken? Was he with you?\"","Damien nodded without taking his eyes off the demons.","\"Yes. We met during the exam. He tried to get away from me, but we ran into these demons.\"","Botis chuckled softly.","\"Oh? Your friend?\" He shrugged. \"He slipped away... leaving you behind.\"","He put pressure on his leg, ready to attack at students, but just then.","Click.","The crisp sound of a sword sliding back into its scabbard echoed through the forest.","Botis’s expression changed instantly. His instincts screamed.","Without even looking toward the source, he immediately ducked.","Whisssh!","A razor-thin silver slash shot across the battlefield from the demons’ right side.","The left side from Noah’s and the others’ perspective.","The slash narrowly missed Botis’s head.","Slash!","The enormous tree standing beside him was cut cleanly in half.","A heartbeat later.","BOOM!!","The gigantic trunk crashed onto the forest floor, shaking the surrounding ground.","Dust, leaves, and broken branches exploded into the air.","Noah, Damien, Kaelan, and Myra quickly retreated several steps to avoid the falling tree.","The battlefield was soon covered in drifting dust.","Noah coughed lightly.","\"Cough...\"","He already knew who had launched that attack.","His eyes immediately searched toward the left side of their formation. The direction from which the slash had come.","\"Ken?\"","As the dust slowly settled, a lone figure emerged from between the towering trees.","It was Ken.","He stood quietly with a black scabbard hanging at his waist.","His sword had already been returned inside it.","His expression remained as calm as ever, as though he had merely taken a casual stroll through the forest rather than launching an attack capable of cutting down a massive tree.","His crimson eyes remained fixed on Ken.","\"...Interesting,\" he muttered. \"I nearly died from that attack.\"","Ken stood there calmly with one hand resting on the hilt of his sheathed sword.","Ken’s eyes were cold. There was no other expression. No fear, no tension...only cold calculation.","He straightened his posture while keeping his spear lowered.","\"Good thing my instincts warned me in time.\"","His gaze remained locked on Ken. \"I would have lost my head otherwise.\"","Ken remained silent. His expression did not change in the slightest.","The only response he gave was tightening his fingers around the hilt of his sword.","Damien glanced at Noah.","\"What should we do?\"","Noah never took his eyes off the demons.","\"We fight.\"","Damien nodded.","While Noah asked, \"Can you handle one demon alone?\"","Damien answered without hesitation. \"I can handle one of the two behind him.\"","His gaze shifted toward Botis. \"But the demon name Botis... he’s too strong.\"","Noah quickly assessed the battlefield. There were four of them.","They were four students and three demons.","Botis was clearly the strongest among them.","Noah made his decision immediately.","\"Alright.\"","He pointed toward the two demons standing behind Botis.","\"Mary and I will take one.\"","He looked toward Damien.","\"You take the other.\"","Finally, his eyes landed on Kaelan and Ken.","\"You Kaelan, you fight Botis together with Ken.\"","He spoke seriously. \"I think the two of you have the best chance against him.\"","Kaelan gave a firm nod.","Ken on other side remained silent, but he stepped forward.","That alone was enough of an answer that he was already prepared to fight.","Botis finally turned his face and quietly watched them divide themselves before chuckling.","\"So you’ve already assigned your opponents.\"","He slowly spun his spear once.","\"How thoughtful.\"","Behind him, Xavier stepped forward and unsheathed his sword.","\"Botis.\"","His voice was cold.","\"Let’s kill them.\"","Daniel also drew his weapon.","\"We don’t have much time.\"","His eyes briefly moved toward the dead body lying several meters away.","\"Caim is dead.\"","His expression darkened.","\"We’ve already lost one.\"","Botis clicked his tongue.","\"What a disappointment.\"","He slowly raised his spear. \"Then let’s finish this quickly.\"","Noah tightened his grip around his own spear before shouting,","\"Mary! Come with me!\"","Without another word, he burst forward. Mary immediately followed behind him with her wand already glowing.","At the same moment Damien dashed toward Daniel.","Kaelan charged directly at Botis. Ken silently vanished from his spot.","Everything happened at once. Botis reacted instantly.","His spear flashed upward.","Clang!","Kaelan’s twin daggers collided against the demon’s weapon.","The impact echoed throughout the forest.","Kaelan’s feet dug into the ground as he absorbed the force.","Botis smirked.","\"You came back for another beating.\"","Kaelan answered by twisting both daggers and launching another flurry of attacks.","Meanwhile, Damien changed direction midway.","Instead of joining Kaelan, he shot straight toward Daniel.","\"Ken!\"","Damien shouted without slowing down.","\"Help Kaelan!\"","Ken did not reply. His body blurred before appearing beside Botis.","Without hesitation, he drew his sword and put it inside.","For many, it felt like he never draw his sword out.","But his movement was just so fast that no one notice it expect Botis.","Click.","A razor-thin silver arc flashed through the air.","Botis’s instincts screamed. He immediately leaned backward.","Whoosh!","The slash narrowly missed his face before continuing into the forest.","Several towering trees behind him were sliced cleanly in half.","Boom!","The massive trunks crashed onto the ground, sending dust and broken branches flying in every direction.","Botis looked at Ken with a far more serious expression than before.","\"...That attack again.\"","For the first time since arriving he no longer looked relaxed.","Even though he was stronger... one wrong movement and he was dead.","Kaelan took advantage of the brief distraction.","Darkness gathered around both daggers before he slashed in a cross pattern.","Two black crescent blades tore toward Botis. The demon spun his spear.","Dark mana exploded around its shaft.","Boom!","The darkness attacks shattered apart.","However, Ken had already disappeared again.","Botis’s pupils contracted.","He sensed behind me. He spun around instantly.","Clang!","Ken’s blade struck against the shaft of the spear.","Sparks erupted. Neither side moved.","For a brief moment their eyes met.","Botis smiled. \"You’re dangerous.\"","Ken calmly pushed his blade away before retreating several steps. Not a single unnecessary movement. Not a single wasted breath.","Botis finally understood. Among all the students present. This silent young man could become biggest danger.","---","Several dozen meters away..","Noah and Mary had already reached Xavier.","The demon calmly rested his sword over one shoulder as he watched the two approach.","A faint smile appeared on his lips.","\"So...\"","His gaze shifted between them. \"My opponents are just children.\"","He slowly lowered his sword. \"I was hoping for someone stronger.\"","Noah smiled back. \"Don’t underestimate children.\"","Blue mana quietly flowed around his sword.","Beside him, Mary raised her wand as orange flames began gathering around its crystal.","The air gradually grew hotter.","Xavier’s smile widened.","\"Perfect.\"","He lowered into a fighting stance.","\"Come.\"","The battle began."]},{"number":187,"title":"Chapter 187: Xavier (1)","paragraphs":["Clang!!","Noah’s sword collided head-on with Xavier’s.","The instant the blades met, Noah’s expression changed.","\"Argh!\"","A terrifying force surged through his arms.","’He’s stronger...!’","His feet slid several meters across the ground, carving deep trails through the soil before he managed to stop himself.","His fingers tightened around the sword. ’He’s at the Condensed Core Realm... Low Rank... maybe even Mid Rank. Dammit!’","Noah quickly glanced at Myra. \"Mary! Let’s draw him away!\"","She immediately understood his intention.","\"Got it!\"","The two of them dashed deeper into the forest. Branches whipped past their faces as they sprinted between the giant trees.","Behind them he came.","Boom!","Xavier kicked off the ground. His speed exploded. Within only a few seconds, he had already closed the distance.","\"So slow.\"","His cold voice came from directly behind Noah.","Noah instantly spun around.","Clang!","Their swords collided once again. This time, deep blue lightning surged across Xavier’s blade.","Crackle!","Violent currents exploded through Noah’s sword.","\"ARGHH!\"","Electricity rushed through his arms, making every muscle twitch violently. The numbness spread toward his shoulder.","Noah immediately threw himself backward before Xavier’s follow-up strike could reach him.","He landed several meters away and exhaled heavily.","’Troublesome...Lightning Affinity.’","The crackling mana around Xavier’s weapon wasn’t merely increasing its cutting power.Every clash sent electricity through Noah’s body, slowly numbing his muscles.","Xavier smiled faintly.","\"You’ve got decent instincts. But that’s all.\"","He vanished again.","\"So fast!\"","Noah barely managed to react.","Clang!","Clang!","Clang!","Three consecutive strikes rained down without giving Noah a chance to breathe. Each impact forced him farther backward.","His arms began trembling from the accumulated force.","’He’s overwhelming me...’","Just then he asked for help.","\"Mary!\"","A golden magic circle appeared beneath Noah’s feet.","Warm orange light enveloped his body.","[Strength Enhancement]","Mana flowed into his limbs. The soreness in his muscles lessened. His physical strength noticeably increased.","\"I’ve boosted your strength!\" Mary shouted.","\"Good!\"","She raised her wand.","A crimson magic circle rapidly formed before her.","[Fire Lance]","Three blazing spears condensed in the air before shooting toward Xavier.","Whoosh!","Whoosh!","Whoosh!","Xavier didn’t even stop moving.","His sword flashed.","Slash!","Slash!","Slash!","Each fire lance split cleanly in half before exploding harmlessly behind him.","Boom!","Boom!","Boom!","The surrounding trees shook from the explosions.","Noah didn’t waste the opportunity.","Dozens of sharp ice spikes erupted from the ground beneath Xavier’s feet.","Crack!","Crack!","Crack!","The spikes pierced upward from every direction.","Xavier calmly leaped into the air. The ice shattered beneath him.","Before he landed. Noah was already waiting. His sword became coated in beautifully compressed blue ice. Cold mist spread around the blade. He swung with all his strength.","Clang!","Xavier blocked the strike effortlessly with one hand. A grin appeared on the demon’s face.","\"So this is your Ice magic? Not bad. But too weak.\"","Blue lightning suddenly exploded from his sword.","Boom!","Noah’s frozen blade cracked under the impact. His entire body was blasted backward. He crashed into the trunk of a massive tree.","Boom!","The tree shook violently.","\"Ghk!\"","Blood spilled from the corner of Noah’s mouth.","Before he could recover from it, Xavier was already in front of him.","He was too fast.","Noah instinctively raised his sword.","Clang!","Another heavy strike slammed into it. His knees bent under the overwhelming pressure. The ground beneath his boots fractured.","Crack!","Noah gritted his teeth. ’Even with Myra’s enhancement...I’m still losing in pure strength.’","Mary pointed her wand toward Xavier. A massive crimson magic circle formed overhead.","[Blazing Meteor]","A gigantic sphere of fire roared toward the demon. The surrounding temperature rose sharply.","Xavier clicked his tongue. Without even looking back, he swung his free hand. A bolt of blue lightning burst from his palm.","Boom!!","The fireball exploded in midair. A wave of heat swept across the forest. Smoke engulfed the battlefield.","Noah immediately took advantage of the cover. More than twenty ice swords materialized around him. Their razor-sharp tips pointed directly at Xavier.","\"Go!\"","The weapons shot forward from every direction.","At the same time the surface beneath them turned into ice.","Whoosh!","Whoosh!","Whoosh!","Yet Xavier’s body blurred.","He weaved effortlessly between the incoming blades.","One sword after another missed by mere centimeters.","The few that reached him. Shattered beneath his lightning-covered blade.","The ice surface that was spreading over ground shattered the movement Xavier’s feet covered with lightning stomp over it.","Crack!","Crack!","Crack!","Fragments of ice scattered across the forest floor.","When the last sword broke. Xavier had already reached Noah once again.","He drove his knee into Noah’s abdomen.","Boom!","\"Cough!\"","The air was forced out of Noah’s lungs. Blood splattered from his mouth. His body folded before being sent flying across the ground. He rolled several times before finally stopping.","His breathing became ragged.","His arms trembled.","His muscles ached from blocking so many powerful blows.","Xavier slowly walked toward him, lightning crackling around his sword.","\"You’ve done well for someone beneath the Condensed Core Realm.\"","His smile widened.","\"But this battle was decided the moment we crossed blades.\"","Mary attacked from behind him. She thrust her wand forward. Two magic circles appeared simultaneously before her.","One blazed crimson. The other shone with brilliant golden-white light.","[Flame Burst]","[Light Spear]","A massive fireball and a radiant spear of condensed light shot toward Xavier from opposite angles.","The demon frowned.","\"Tch.\"","He abandoned Noah for the moment and spun around. His sword flashed.","Slash!","The fireball split into two before exploding.","Boom!!","A wave of scorching heat swept through the forest. Without pausing, Xavier swung his blade again.","Clang!","The spear of light shattered into countless glowing particles upon colliding with his lightning-covered sword.","The brilliant fragments rained across the forest like tiny stars.","\"Is that all?\" Xavier asked coldly.","Myra bit her lip. She knew neither spell had been powerful enough to injure him.","They had only served one purpose, it was to distract him.","Meanwhile Noah forced himself back onto his feet. His chest ached. His arms still trembled from the previous clashes. Even so, his blue eyes remained calm.","’Now.’","He slammed his palm against the frozen ground. Mana surged from his core.","The ground beneath them trembled violently.","Crack!","Crack!","Crack!","Huge spikes of solid ice burst from beneath the earth."]},{"number":188,"title":"Chapter 188: Xavier (2)","paragraphs":["Instead of erupting immediately beneath Xavier, they raced underground first, tearing through the frozen surface like enormous sharks swimming beneath the sea.","The frozen path rapidly advanced toward the demon.","They were one meter, the five meters, then ten meters.","The earth split apart behind it.","Xavier sensed the danger. His eyes widened slightly.","\"The ground?\"","Boom!!","A gigantic ice spike erupted directly beneath him.","Xavier instantly jumped backward. The spike narrowly missed his body, tearing through empty air.","But Noah had already anticipated it.","Boom!","Boom!","Boom!","A second spike erupted, then a third, then a fourth.","Massive pillars of razor-sharp ice burst from the earth one after another, chasing Xavier relentlessly across the battlefield.","Each eruption shattered rocks and uprooted patches of earth. The surrounding temperature plummeted as frost spread in every direction.","Xavier’s expression finally turned serious.","\"Hmph.\"","Lightning exploded around his legs. His movements became even faster.","Every time an ice spike erupted beneath him, he leaped away at the last possible moment. The forest echoed with continuous explosions.","Boom!","Boom!","Boom!!","Towering pillars of ice pierced toward the sky, leaving behind a devastated trail of shattered earth and frozen trees.","Noah narrowed his eyes which were glowing in glacier color beautiful.","’He’s avoiding every single one...’","His breathing grew heavier. The continuous use of Ice Creation consumed mana far faster than ordinary spells.","Sweat rolled down his forehead. Even so, he didn’t stop.","The ice spikes continued pursuing Xavier without giving him a single moment to rest.","Finally the demon had been forced completely onto the defensive.","Finally, Noah stopped using his Ice Creation ability. His breathing had become heavy, and beads of sweat rolled down his forehead.","’I’ve used too much mana...’","Without hesitation, he stored his sword inside his storage ring and pulled out his spear. The familiar blue-and-silver weapon appeared in his hand.","He tightened his grip. A thin layer of compressed ice slowly spread across the spearhead, making the weapon glow with a beautiful icy blue radiance.","His first blade technique have ability to burst or spread ice with each slash or attack. he was using that on spear.","Cold mist drifted from its blade. Noah took a deep breath. Then he hurled the spear with all his strength.","Whoosh!!","The spear tore through the freezing air with a sharp whistling sound, spinning rapidly as it flew toward Xavier. Its icy aura left a faint trail of frost behind it.","Xavier landed lightly on the ground. His eyes immediately locked onto the incoming weapon.","\"Hmph.\"","Blue lightning erupted around his sword. Without hesitation, he swung.","BOOM!!","The lightning-covered blade collided directly with the spear. A violent burst of blue lightning exploded outward.","But at that exact moment.","Crack!","The layer of compressed ice coating Noah’s spear suddenly detonated.","A surge of freezing mana erupted from within it.","Blue ice and deep-blue lightning collided together, creating a strange azure explosion that swallowed Xavier.","BOOM!!","A shockwave swept across the surrounding forest. Several nearby trees shook violently. Chunks of frozen earth scattered in every direction.","When the smoke cleared. Xavier stood there with several fresh cuts across his arms and shoulder.","His battle clothes had been torn in a few places. Thin streaks of blood slowly dripped onto the frozen ground.","His expression darkened. At that same moment.","Mary raised her wand. Another blazing fire spell shot toward Xavier. A massive sphere of flames roared across the battlefield.","Xavier’s cold eyes shifted toward her. \"You’ve become annoying.\"","A blue magic circle instantly formed before his hand.","[Lightning Bolt]","A bolt of compressed lightning burst forward.","Boom!!","The two spells collided in midair before exploding. The violent shockwave forced Myra back several steps.","Before she could recover, Xavier disappeared.","His body became nothing more than a streak of blue lightning.","Noah’s eyes widened and the next instant,","Clang!!","Xavier’s sword descended toward Noah’s neck. Noah barely managed to block it with another ice sword he had created.","The impact threw him backward. Before he regained his balance.","Xavier attacked again.","Slash!","Slash!","Slash!","His sword became nothing more than flashes of blue light. Each strike came from a different angle. Noah desperately dodged.","Some attacks missed by only a few centimeters. Others left shallow cuts across his shoulders, arms, and chest.","Blood slowly stained his academy battle gear.","\"Ghk!\"","Another slash grazed his ribs. Pain spread through his body. His body felt like it was burning.","His muscles had already become sluggish from the lightning flowing through every clash.","Meanwhile Xavier suddenly changed targets. His figure blurred toward Myra.","She hastily raised several fire barriers.","Boom!","Boom!","Boom!","Each barrier shattered after a single strike. A shallow cut appeared across her left arm. Another slash tore across her thigh.","She stumbled backward, breathing heavily. The difference in strength had become overwhelming.","This time Xavier intended to go all out. Blue lightning exploded around his entire body.","His speed increased even further. He moved like a bolt of lightning weaving through the forest.","Neither Noah nor Myra could keep up anymore. Every exchange ended with another wound. Another burst of pain. Another step backward.","Noah clenched his teeth. ’At this rate... we’ll both die.’","He looked toward Myra.","She was exhausted. Her breathing had become ragged. Blood dripped from several wounds across her body.","Noah made his decision.","\"Mary!\"","She instinctively looked toward him.","\"Run!\"","She froze for a moment.","\"What?\"","\"I’ll hold him back!\"","\"Noah—\"","\"Go!\"","His voice was louder than before.","\"Trust me!\"","Mary bit her lower lip. For a brief second, she hesitated.","Then she nodded.","\"...Alright.\"","She immediately turned and sprinted deeper into the forest.","Xavier noticed. \"You think she can escape?\"","He prepared to chase after her. But Noah thrust both hands toward the ground. Mana surged from his core.","Crack!","Crack!","Crack!!","Towering walls of solid ice erupted around Xavier from every direction.","Within a single heartbeat, a gigantic cage of thick ice imprisoned the demon. The frozen walls rose several meters into the air.","Noah didn’t wait to see the result. His bloodied body turned around. He immediately sprinted after Myra.","Each step sent pain through his wounded muscles. Behind him a terrifying amount of blue lightning erupted.","BOOM!!","The entire ice prison exploded apart.","Countless frozen fragments flew through the forest.","Xavier emerged from the shattered cage with an expression colder than before.","\"You won’t escape.\"","Blue lightning exploded beneath his feet. The demon shot after the fleeing pair like a flash of lightning.","And the situation with Damien and others were not much different.","Meanwhile Mary and Noah were unknowingly running in the same direction where the ancient ruin was hidden beneath the earth."]},{"number":189,"title":"Chapter 189: Damien’s Side","paragraphs":["BOOM!!","A body shot through the forest like a cannonball before crashing violently into the trunk of a massive tree.","Thud! Damien’s body slid down the cracked trunk before landing heavily on the ground.","\"Cough!\"","A mouthful of blood escaped his lips. Without wasting even a second, he planted his sword into the earth and forced himself back onto his feet.","His breathing had become rough. Several cuts covered his arms, and his academy battle gear had been torn apart in multiple places.","The young man glared ahead with unwavering determination. Standing nearly twenty meters away, Daniel remained completely composed.","Not a single visible injury covered the demon’s body. His tanned skin glistened beneath the fading evening sunlight as brown mana slowly flowed around both of his fists.","Daniel relied entirely on his fists and earth magic. The surrounding ground trembled slightly beneath his feet.","The evening sun had already begun sinking below the horizon. Long shadows stretched across the forest.","In less than an hour, darkness would completely cover the battlefield.","Daniel calmly looked at Damien.","\"I expected more from you... with a confidence you attacked me.\"","His voice carried neither mockery nor anger.","Damien tightened his grip around his sword. Golden mana surged from his core, flowing through every vein in his body before wrapping around the blade.","The sword emitted a brilliant golden radiance.","\"...I’m not done yet.\"","Daniel slowly clenched his right fist.","Large chunks of stone rose from the ground before rapidly compressing around his gauntlet. Layer after layer of rock wrapped around his arm until it resembled a gigantic stone hammer.","The surrounding air became heavier.","\"You should stay down.\"","Boom!","The demon vanished.","\"So fast!\"","Damien’s pupils shrank. He instinctively swung his sword toward his right.","Clang!!","Golden steel collided against solid stone. A violent shockwave erupted from the impact.","Crack!","The ground beneath Damien’s feet fractured instantly. His entire body shook violently.","\"Ghk!\"","His arms trembled from the overwhelming strength behind Daniel’s punch.","The demon smiled faintly. \"You are too slow., young man\"","His left fist came flying toward Damien’s ribs.","Boom!!","The stone-covered punch landed squarely against Damien’s side.","\"Cough!\"","Blood sprayed from Damien’s mouth. His body was launched sideways before smashing through two thick trees.","Wood shattered everywhere. He rolled several times across the forest floor before forcing himself upright once more.","His ribs throbbed painfully.","’I blocked it...Yet it still did this much damage.’","Daniel slowly walked toward him.","Each step remained calm. As though he wasn’t fighting the academy’s strongest first-year student.","Brown mana suddenly gathered beneath Damien’s feet.","His instincts screamed. Without hesitation, he jumped backward.","Boom!","Several enormous stone spikes erupted from the ground where he had been standing only a heartbeat earlier.","The jagged pillars pierced several meters into the air. Damien landed on another patch of ground. Only to get ready for another spell. Another magic circle had already formed beneath him.","\"Damn it!\"","Boom!","More stone pillars burst upward as Damien leaped again. They erupted again and then again. One explosion followed another. The battlefield became filled with towering spikes of rock.","Daniel calmly controlled every spell without moving from his position.","Damien gritted his teeth. ’He’s controlling the battlefield...I can’t even get close.’","The moment his feet finally touched solid ground.","Daniel appeared before him.","Boom!","A massive stone fist descended toward Damien’s face. Damien immediately raised his glowing sword.","Clang!!","Golden mana exploded outward. The collision shook the surrounding forest. Even though Damien blocked the attack. His knees bent under the tremendous force.","Crack!","The earth beneath him shattered into countless fractures.","His muscles screamed.","Daniel looked directly into Damien’s eyes.","\"Still standing?\"","Without warning, his knee slammed into Damien’s abdomen.","Boom!","\"Gah!\"","The air was forced from Damien’s lungs. Before his body could even react, Daniel’s elbow crashed into his shoulder.","Crack!","Damien lost his balance. Another punch struck his chest.","Boom!!","His body flew backward once more. This time he rolled nearly twenty meters before finally stopping. Dust slowly settled around him. His breathing had become noticeably heavier.","Blood trickled down his chin. His left arm had begun trembling uncontrollably.","’He’s...Far stronger than me.’","Yet Damien refused to stay down. He slowly stood again. Golden mana continued flowing around his sword.","His eyes never left Daniel.","The demon sighed.","\"I’ll admit it. Your determination is impressive. But determination doesn’t close the gap between our realms.\"","Damien smiled faintly.","\"...Who said I was trying to close it?\"","Daniel raised an eyebrow.","The next instant Golden light erupted around Damien.","His sword shone brighter than ever before. The surrounding darkness was momentarily pushed away.","Sword Art...","[Heavenly Sacred Radiance.]","A five star sword art that Damien posses. It was different from Noah Frozen Lotus Blade Art.","Whereas Noah’s blade art have eight forms, Damien’s sword art only have six.","But his sword art was more focus on attacking power and destruction. It was explosive. Unlike how Noah have cold and calm blade art. That involves frost. Opposite to heat.","The golden aura condensed around the blade. Damien slowly raised his sword vertically before his face.","His expression became perfectly calm. The surrounding mana trembled.","Daniel narrowed his eyes.","\"...Interesting.\"","Damien inhaled deeply. For this attack he activated his Solar Core Ability. Which boost his powers.","His body disappeared.","Boom!","A streak of radiant golden light flashed across the battlefield. The sword descended with terrifying momentum.","[First Form— Shinkō Issen: Radiant Severance.]","A gigantic vertical slash of condensed golden light cleaved through the forest. Trees split apart effortlessly. The earth itself divided beneath the attack.","Daniel’s expression finally became serious. Brown mana exploded around his body. Several massive slabs of rock erupted before him.","Boom!","The golden slash cut through the first wall, then the second and then the third. Rock after rock shattered beneath the overwhelming radiance.","Daniel thrust both fists forward simultaneously. Earth and rocks rose from ground forming a layer upon him. Like a strong armor which he covered with strong brown Mana.","Boom!!","The attack finally collided against his stone gauntlets. The entire battlefield shook violently.","Daniel’s body was slide behind from attack.","Crack.","Fractures spread across Daniel’s rocky armor.","Crack.","They shattered completely.","His eyebrows rose slightly. he’s body felt numb after taking that attack. He could even feel pain.","\"haha..Not bad.\"","But it was enough to defeat the demon. He was at condensed core low or maybe mid.","The next instant, brown mana erupted explosively from his body.","Boom!!","Damien had used his ability to boost his power and then used his first form of sword art. He used most of his power in it. The mana outburst from Daniel was strong for him.","He spun helplessly through the air before crashing onto the forest floor.","Thud!","His sword slipped from his grasp before embedding itself into the dirt several meters away.","Damien struggled to breathe. His vision blurred slightly.","His muscles had reached their limit. Fighting for exam all day, then meeting this demon, fighting them and then survived somehow. Only to meet Noah and others. Then once again fighting same demon.","Daniel slowly walked toward him.","The stone around his fists began reforming.","\"You’ve earned my respect.\"","He stopped a few meters away.","\"So I’ll end this quickly.\""]},{"number":190,"title":"Chapter 190: Arrived Just In Time","paragraphs":["A gigantic magic circle spread beneath his feet. Brown mana flooded into the formation. The surrounding earth began trembling violently. Large boulders floated into the air.","They compressed together above Daniel’s right fist until an enormous rocky gauntlet several times larger than before had formed.","The sheer pressure distorted the surrounding air.","Damien stared at it while lying on one knee.","’...This attack.’","He forced himself toward his fallen sword. His fingers barely touched the hilt.","’I need to formed sun blast from my ability.’","The reason why Damien still haven’t use it was simple. If he used it then he couldn’t fight any further. That means he could not go back to Kaelan and Ken to help them.","A thought came to him, if he had fought that Botis alone. But again he was stronger that Daniel. Damien might been dead before he could use his ability.","Daniel disappeared.","Boom!","He appeared directly before Damien. The gigantic stone fist descended toward his head. Just before the crushing blow landed.","Whoosh!!","A brilliant lance of golden light shot across the battlefield.","Daniel’s instincts reacted instantly. His eyes widened. He abandoned the attack without hesitation and jumped backward.","Boom!!","The radiant lance struck the ground where he had been standing. A blinding explosion of golden light erupted.","Dust and shattered earth flew everywhere.","Daniel narrowed his eyes toward the source.","\"...Another one.\"","Damien slowly turned as well. A figure sprinted through the forest.","Long golden-blonde hair danced behind her. Pink eyes shone with determination.","In her hand rested a magnificent golden spear wrapped in radiant mana. She stopped beside Damien and pointed her spear toward Daniel.","Without taking her eyes off the demon, she looked at him with worried eyes.","\"It seems...I arrived just in time.\"","She was Lyria.","---","Some distance away from them.","The battle against Botis had become even more desperate.","CLANG!!","Ken’s slender longsword collided against Botis’s spear.","Orange flames erupted around the spearhead. The tremendous force pushed Ken backward several meters.","His boots dug deep trenches into the forest floor. Before he could regain his footing.","Botis vanished.","Ken barely raised his blade.","CLANG!!","The spear thrust struck his sword with terrifying precision. The impact numbed both of his arms.","Botis spun the spear effortlessly before sweeping it horizontally.","Ken ducked beneath the flaming blade. The burning edge passed just above his head, scorching several strands of his dark hair.","At that exact moment, Kaelan appeared behind Botis. Darkness wrapped around both daggers.","He unleashed a rapid flurry of slashes. Black streaks cut through the air.","Botis didn’t even look behind him. He simply rotated his spear.","CLANG!","CLANG!","CLANG!","Every dagger strike was blocked flawlessly.","\"What incredible technique...\" Kaelan muttered.","Botis smirked.","\"You’re have keen eyes.\"","The spear suddenly changed direction. Instead of attacking Ken. It shot directly toward Kaelan’s chest.","It was too fast.","Kaelan’s pupils shrank. He instinctively crossed both daggers.","CLANG!!","The spearhead pierced through the gap between them. It stopped only inches away from his heart.","The overwhelming force launched Kaelan backward. He rolled across the ground before barely managing to stand. Blood trickled from his mouth.","Botis immediately pursued him.","\"You’re my target.\"","Orange flames intensified around his spear. He thrust once, then twice and then third time. Every attack targeted Kaelan’s vital organs.","Botis aim for his chest, neck and stomach. Each thrust carried absolute killing intent.","Kaelan desperately parried using both daggers. His Black star ability helps him to reduce the strength of each strike by absorbing mana from it.","Sweat dripped from his forehead. His wrists were beginning to ache. His muscles screamed from the continuous impacts.","Every strike became harder to block.","If Kaelan was fighting alone, he had been dead by now. But because of Ken, he was save many times.","Ken suddenly appeared beside Botis. His sword disappeared into its sheath.","His body lowered.","Click.","The blade left the scabbard. A single silver line flashed across the battlefield.","Botis reacted instantly.","His spear intercepted the attack.","CLANG!!","Even so a thin cut appeared across Botis’s shoulder.","Blood slowly trickled down.","Botis glanced at the wound before smiling.","His spear burst into flames once again. He spun around violently. A circular wave of blazing fire exploded outward.","Ken and Kaelan were both forced backward. The surrounding trees ignited immediately.","Heat filled the battlefield. Botis lunged again.","This time he completely ignored Ken. His eyes remained fixed only on Kaelan. The spear shot forward like a blazing dragon.","Kaelan’s instincts screamed. He activated Black Star.","Dark attraction spread around him. Loose mana began flowing toward his body.","The incoming spear weakened. Only slightly, so it wasn’t enough. The flaming spearhead broke through his defense. It continued straight toward his chest.","’I can’t stop it...!’ Just before the spear pierced his heart.","WHOOSH!!","A sharp whistle echoed through the forest.","Botis’s instincts suddenly flared. Without hesitation, he withdrew his spear and stepped backward.","A split second later.","BOOM!!","An arrow wrapped in violently rotating wind slammed into the ground where he had been standing. The explosion carved a deep crater into the earth.","Powerful gusts scattered dust and burning leaves everywhere.","Botis narrowed his eyes.","\"...Another one?\"","Everyone instinctively looked upward. Standing upon the thick branch of a towering tree...","Was a young woman. Long violet hair fluttered behind her in the evening wind.","Golden-yellow eyes glowed brilliantly. She calmly held a beautifully crafted bow.","Another arrow had already been nocked. Green wind mana spiraled around its tip.","She looked directly at Botis. \"You’ll have to face me as well.\"","Kaelan stared upward in surprise.","\"...An archer?\"","Ken allowed himself a small smile.","\"Good timing.\"","---","Back to Noah and Mary.","The Demon name Xavier followed them and then he came to a clearing. It was small space with huge trees surrounded to it. Waist length grass was grown over the ground.","Xavier stood there, he was thinking that Noah and Mary must have been hidden somewhere here.","The grass was big enough for a person to hide. He raised his hand above, a huge blue color magic circle started to formed.","He was going to attack at every corner of the place. But just then he felt huge mana moving under him.","It was same feeling like before when the young man with white hair had created ice pillars from beneath the ground.","\"Shitt!\""]},{"number":191,"title":"Chapter 191: Using His Ability to the Fullest","paragraphs":["\"Shit!!\"","Xavier bent his knees before explosively launching himself high into the air.","CRAAACKKK!!","A gigantic ice spike erupted from the ground where he had been standing. It didn’t stop there. The massive spike continued growing, chasing Xavier upward like a living pillar of ice.","\"Tch... Annoying.\"","Blue lightning burst from Xavier’s body.","BOOM!","The ice spike shattered into countless frozen fragments. Yet before he could catch his breath.","CRACK! CRACK! CRACK!","More colossal spikes erupted from the earth from every direction. Each one twisted upward, relentlessly pursuing him through the air.","They rose one after another, forming a deadly forest of jagged ice that sought to impale him.","\"Dammit!\"","A short distance away. Noah remained hidden within the tall grass, kneeling low with his breathing ragged.","Slowly, he rose to his feet. In his hands rested a spear forged entirely from pure ice. Its translucent shaft shimmered with a beautiful glacier-blue glow beneath the fading evening light.","Tiny frozen spikes covered the grip where his hands rested, allowing him to maintain a firm hold despite the moisture from melting frost.","The surrounding temperature continued to plummet.","His veins throbbed violently beneath his skin.","Mana poured out of his body at an alarming rate.","During his retreat, he had already consumed two Mana Recovery Potions and a Healing Potion.","They had eased his condition only slightly. His reserves were depleting faster than ever with how much he eas using his ability.","\"...Just a little more.\"","He forced even more mana through his core.","Pain shot throughout his entire body. Blood slowly trickled from the corner of his mouth.","Even so he refused to stop.","BOOM!","He kicked off the ground with all his strength. The earth beneath his feet shattered.","His body shot forward like an arrow. As he sprinted, another massive ice spike erupted ahead of him, rising diagonally toward the sky.","Without slowing down, Noah stepped onto it. The enormous pillar continued growing while carrying him higher into the air.","It was as though he were running along a rapidly rising frozen bridge.","Xavier landed atop another ice pillar. He immediately spotted Noah charging straight toward him from another spike.","The young man’s glacier-blue eyes glowed brilliantly, leaving faint icy trails behind every movement.","Cold mist escaped with every breath he took. The air around them had become bitterly cold.","Frost spread across the surrounding trees.","Xavier narrowed his eyes.","\"So you’re making this your battlefield...\"","Lightning exploded from his body. Blue arcs danced wildly around him. The crackling electricity shattered every incoming spike before it could reach him.","Ice burst apart one after another.","Still Noah continued advancing without hesitation. Blood now leaked not only from his mouth. Thin crimson trails also flowed from the corners of his eyes.","His body had begun reaching its limit. Yet his feet never slowed.","Only one thought remained in his mind.","’Defeat him.’","The darkness of evening had already settled across the forest. Only the faint orange glow of the setting sun lingered beyond the horizon.","Against that dim backdrop, Xavier resembled a living bolt of lightning.","His lightning reflected against the crystal like ice spike. Which brightened the dark forest beautifully.","His sword blazed with dazzling blue thunder. Every swing released arcs of electricity that blasted apart the incoming ice.","Noah finally closed the distance. He planted his left foot firmly upon the frozen pillar.","His right arm drew the spear back over his shoulder. Cold mana roared around it like a raging winter blizzard.","His muscles tightened. Then he threw it with all his strength.","WHISSHHHH!!","The spear shot forward like a glacier-blue comet. The air screamed as it tore through it.","Its target,Xavier.","The distance between them was barely several meters.","Xavier calmly stepped forward. Lightning exploded beneath his feet.","In an instant he vanished from his position. Like a flash of blue thunder, he appeared directly before the incoming spear.","He landed lightly upon the very ice pillar Noah was sprinting across.","The spear was already upon him. His sword moved.","It was So fast that Noah couldn’t even follow the motion.","CLANG!!","The brilliant lightning-covered blade sliced through the ice spear effortlessly. It shattered into thousands of glittering frozen fragments.","A confident smile spread across Xavier’s face.","\"So that’s your trump card?\"","He raised his sword.","\"That’s it, young man.\"","Noah’s expression never changed. He continued charging forward. His left hand stretched outward.","He opened his palm.","His cold eyes remained fixed upon Xavier. Then he clenched his fist.","The countless fragments produced from the shattered spear suddenly changed direction. They accelerated toward Xavier from every side.","Like a deadly blizzard of razor-sharp ice.","SHHHHH!!","The frozen shards slammed into the lightning surrounding Xavier. Blue electricity immediately began vaporizing them.","One after another.","But Noah had never intended them to pierce through. He only needed them to get close. The instant the fragments surrounded Xavier.","BOOM!!","Every shard exploded into freezing mist.","An enormous cloud of frost swallowed the demon completely.","For the first time Xavier’s eyes widened.","\"...What?\"","Frost rapidly clung to his light armor beneath the cloak, his clothes, his skin.","His movements slowed ever so slightly.","And that single moment was all Noah needed.","He was already there. Only a single step separated them.","Xavier ignored the frost spreading across his body. He swung his sword downward.","The strike was unbelievably fast.","Even Noah’s eyes couldn’t completely follow it.","But he sensed its trajectory. Instead of retreating, he abruptly leaned his entire upper body backward.","SLASH!!","The lightning blade tore across his chest. A deep crimson wound opened instantly.","Hot blood sprayed into the freezing air. The attack had nearly cut him in half.","Yet it had missed every vital organ.","Xavier’s confident expression faltered. \"He intentionally took the hit...?\"","Noah ignored the searing pain. Blood poured freely down his chest. With a wave of his hand, more than thirty ice weapons materialized around him.","They were swords, spears, daggers and axes. They formed in blinked of an eye.","Noah had never made them so fast before.","Each one shimmered with deadly cold.","His shoulders had already become coated in frost.","His arms trembled violently. Even his legs had begun freezing after continuously standing atop the massive ice pillar.","The cold bit deeply into his own flesh. His vision blurred from exhaustion. His body screamed for rest.","Yet...He remained standing. His eyes glowed with an unnatural icy brilliance.","Xavier instinctively felt danger. He felt genuine fear.","Suddenly his focus lost for a brief moment. His vision blurred, his mind become daze. Before he could come out to his own senses.","Noah calmly snapped his fingers.","Snap."]},{"number":192,"title":"Chapter 192: Killing Xavier","paragraphs":["The frozen weapons shot forward simultaneously.","SHCKK!","SHCKK!","SHCKK!","They came from every direction. They were too many and too fast.","\"ARRRGGHHHH!!\"","Several swords pierced through Xavier’s torso. A spear drove through his shoulder.","Two daggers buried themselves deep into his thigh and side.","An axe tore into his upper arm. Blood erupted into the air. His scream echoed throughout the forest.","The demon came out of his darkness.","He stared at Noah in disbelief. The young man remained standing amidst towering pillars of ice.","Blood completely soaked his academy battle gear.","His pale face showed no emotion. His glowing glacier-blue eyes stared silently at the demon.","The battlefield had transformed. Gigantic pillars of ice surrounded them from every direction.","The temperature had dropped to terrifying levels. It felt as though Xavier had stepped into Noah’s frozen domain.","He couldn’t believe how could a young man ay awakened stage do something like this.","With the last of his remaining strength Xavier roared. Blue lightning erupted violently from his body.","He attempted to destroy every weapon lodged inside him.","But Noah slowly raised one hand. Then closed it into a fist. The embedded ice weapons responded instantly.","CRACK!!","Every weapon exploded from within. Massive crystal-like ice spikes burst outward through Xavier’s flesh.","Blood mixed with glittering ice. The spikes erupted through his chest, shoulders, back, and legs.","Xavier coughed violently. Blood poured from his mouth. His heartbeat slowed.","Frost spread rapidly across every wound.","It crawled over his arms..","Across his torso, over his neck and his cheek.","Then it froze His jaw. Finally reached his eyes. The last thing Xavier saw was Noah standing silently before him.","A blood-soaked warrior surrounded by towering glaciers. Then frost completely covered his vision.","Within seconds his entire body became encased in solid ice. He remained frozen in place.","A lifeless statue trapped forever beneath eternal winter.","---","Noah finally lost his balance. The towering pillar of ice beneath his feet began to crack apart.","Crack...","His legs gave out. His exhausted body tumbled from the frozen structure and crashed onto the ground below.","Thud.","\"...Haa... haa...\"","His chest rose and fell violently. Every breath burned his lungs.","The battle had drained nearly all of his mana, and the constant overuse of his Ice Creation ability had pushed both his body and mind to their limits.","For several long seconds, he simply lay there, staring at the dark sky above.","Rustle.","From several meters away, where a patch of waist-high grass still remained untouched by the battle, someone emerged.","It was Mary.","She had been hiding there the entire time. Before confronting Xavier, Noah had instructed her to stay hidden no matter what happened.","With her Observation-type ability and exceptionally keen eyesight, she had discovered something unusual beneath the tall grass.","A naturally concealed hollow just large enough for a person to crawl into.","The thick vegetation completely hid its entrance from outside, making it a perfect hiding place.","Trusting Noah’s judgment, she had remained inside while secretly watching the battle unfold through narrow gaps in the grass.","Noah had told her don’t come out unless he gave out.","The moment Xavier died, she rushed out.","\"Noah!\"","She hurried across the frozen battlefield before dropping to her knees beside him.","\"Noah! Are you okay? Noah!\"","Panic filled her voice. Without wasting another second, she raised her wand.","A gentle white magic circle bloomed beneath Noah’s body.","Warm, soothing light flowed over him.","[Healing Light]","The warmth eased the pain coursing through his body. The countless cuts covering his arms and legs slowly began to close.","Even the deep wound across his chest stopped bleeding as torn flesh gradually mended itself.","The healing wasn’t fast enough to restore him completely, but it was more than enough to stabilize his condition.","Noah let out a long breath.","\"...I’m... okay.\"","Mary looked at him through eyes that had already become moist with tears.","\"Why...?\" she asked softly.","\"Why didn’t you let me help?\"","Noah managed a weak smile. \"There wasn’t any need.\"","His breathing remained uneven.","\"And I... wanted to test something.. So fighting alone was good option.\"","He glanced toward Xavier’s frozen corpse. \"I wanted to see... whether I could defeat someone stronger than me using everything I’d learned.\"","Mary frowned.","\"Idiot.\"","There was obvious anger in her voice, but it couldn’t hide the relief she felt.","\"You nearly got yourself killed.\"","Carefully, she slipped one of his arms over her shoulder and helped him to his feet.","His legs trembled the moment he stood.","The two slowly began walking away from the battlefield.","The clearing, once covered with tall grass, had transformed into a frozen wasteland.","Towering pillars of ice still rose toward the night sky.","Frost covered every blade of grass. The temperature remained unnaturally cold.","The last traces of sunset had disappeared.","Darkness had completely claimed the forest.","Only the pale moonlight illuminated their path.","After walking for a short distance. Mary suddenly stopped.","Noah looked at her. \"What happened?\"","She hesitated for a moment before speaking.","Her expression had become strangely nervous.","\"Noah...When I was hiding...\"","She looked back toward the patch of tall grass she had emerged from earlier. \"I don’t think it was just a hiding place.\"","Noah frowned. \"What do you mean?\"","Mary adjusted her glasses.","\"After I climbed into that hollow, I realized it was much deeper than I expected.\"","\"There was a narrow passage leading underground. I... got curious.\"","\"So I walked a little farther inside.\"","She swallowed nervously before continuing. \"The tunnel eventually opened into a stone corridor.\"","\"It looked... artificial. Like it had been built by someone.\"","She paused.","\"And at the end of it...There was somethinh like huge metal door.\"","Noah’s exhausted eyes immediately sharpened.","\"A metal door?\"","Mary nodded.\"It wasn’t an ordinary door. It was enormous... made entirely of black metal. I couldn’t see any handle, but its surface was covered with strange carvings.It looked... ancient. But we knowing you were going to fight demon. I came returned to see your battle.\"","A thoughtful expression appeared on Noah’s face. An underground passage. An ancient metal door hidden underground.","Neither of those should exist in the middle of an uninhabited forest. Which was only filled with monsters.","Something about it immediately felt wrong.","’This place... in this forest there occurred another Act of the game. And if there’s something hidden beneath this place... then it’s not something normal.’","Noah thought seriously."]},{"number":193,"title":"Chapter 193: Hidden Temple","paragraphs":["\"This place really does look ancient.\"","Noah spoke quietly as he walked through the underground passage, leaning on Mary for support.","\"Are you sure about this?\" Mary asked, her voice filled with concern. \"Shouldn’t we check on the others first? Or at least try to find a way to contact the instructors?\"","The two of them were currently exploring the hidden passage Mary had discovered earlier.","Since the examination was expected to last a long time and could require spending nights outdoors, Noah had prepared thoroughly before entering.","His storage ring contained various necessities such as a sleeping bag, cooking utensils, rope, a lighter, and other survival supplies.","One of those items was a torch.","Because Noah possessed only Ice Affinity, he could not create a reliable light source through magic. At the moment, Mary carried the torch in her free hand, its warm orange glow illuminating the darkness around them.","\"Don’t worry,\" Noah replied. \"Damien and the others should be fine... probably.\"","Mary frowned.","\"’Probably’ doesn’t make me feel better.\"","Noah chuckled weakly.","\"Let’s at least take a look at this place first.\"","’As much as I am worried about Damien and others. I am also very curious about this. Also once they kill those demons, I will get notification about reward and end of this Act.’ Noah thought.","Mary sighed. She clearly wanted to argue further, but she knew it would be useless.","Soon they arrived before the massive metal door Mary had mentioned.","The structure was enormous, standing nearly five meters tall. Its dark metallic surface was covered with countless intricate engravings. Ancient symbols, celestial patterns, and unfamiliar runes stretched across the door like a forgotten language from another age.","\"It’s already open,\" Mary said.","Indeed, the door was slightly ajar.","A narrow gap had been left between the two enormous slabs.","\"Let’s go inside.\"","\"Noah, are you absolutely sure?\" Mary asked nervously.","His arm rested over her shoulder as she supported him.","He squeezed her shoulder lightly.","\"It’s just an old ruin. What are you so afraid of?\"","\"That’s exactly why I’m afraid,\" she replied immediately.","Noah could not argue with that. \"Well... let’s find out what’s inside.\"","Together they pushed the door wider.","A low metallic groan echoed through the underground passage.","Creeeeeeak...","The sound seemed unnaturally loud within the silence. Then they stepped inside the darkness.","Click.","Click.","The sound of their footsteps echoed through the darkness.","Noah slowly looked around.","\"This place is beautiful.\"","The floor beneath them was paved with perfectly cut stone slabs that had somehow survived the passage of countless centuries without a single crack.","The walls were crafted from polished stone and decorated with breathtaking carvings.","It was as if they were telling about ancient cities, unknown kings and celestial bodies. But Noah was not archeologist to understand meaning behind them.","There were some strange creatures with wings, horns, and countless eyes. Some resembled dragons.","Others looked like beings that no longer existed in the modern world. Every carving was so detailed that it felt as though the figures might step out of the walls at any moment.","Noah studied everything carefully.","’As worried as I am about Damien and the others...’ he thought, ’...I can’t ignore something like this.’","Mary nodded slowly. \"This place must be thousands of years old.\"","\"It definitely feels that way.\" Noah replied. As they continued deeper into the ruin, another passage appeared ahead.","This one descended downward. A long flight of ancient stone stairs vanished into darkness.","Mary tightened her grip on the torch. \"Alright. Now I’m really starting to get nervous.\"","Noah smiled. \"Why? When I’m right here.\"","\"That’s exactly the problem.\" She replied with worried tone.","\"What?\"","\"You’re injured, exhausted, and barely standing.\"","Noah paused. Her words were true. She was right.","\"...Fair point.\" He couldn’t argue with her.","This was not his past world where the old ruins and building have nothing dangerous expect their weak old structure.","Unlike his previous world, ancient ruins in this world could be extremely dangerous.","Here magic existed. Monsters existed. And even ancient beings existed.","Even forgotten gods and divine beings had once walked this world. Yet despite understanding the danger, Noah could not suppress his curiosity.","If they left now and reported the discovery to the Academy, the entire ruin would likely be sealed off and investigated by experts.","He would never get the chance to learn what secrets were hidden beneath the forest.","Mary saw the look in his eyes. She immediately understood.","The curiosity was winning.","After a long sigh, she shook her head. She couldn’t stop him. He saved her afterall.","\"Fine. Let’s go.\"","Noah’s eyes lit up.","\"Thanks, Mary. You are the best.\"","Together they began descending the stairs.","The deeper they traveled, the colder the air became.","Eventually they reached the bottom.","Both of them stopped. Before them stretched a colossal underground hall.","Towering stone pillars stood in perfect rows on both sides, supporting a ceiling so high that it disappeared into darkness.","Each pillar was covered with ancient runes and artistic engravings. Some depicted stars. Others showed moons, eclipses, and celestial events.","The craftsmanship was beyond anything Noah had ever seen.","\"Wow...\"","Mary stared in amazement. \"This place is far bigger than I expected.\"","Noah nodded. \"I never imagined something like this could be hidden beneath the forest.\"","\"Seems we’ve discovered something incredible.\" Mary said while watching it.","\"We might even get rewarded for it.\"","Despite the pain coursing through his body, Noah couldn’t stop smiling. The two cautiously advanced through the hall, examining everything around them.","The silence felt sacred. As if this place had been untouched for countless ages.","Soon their torchlight fell upon another enormous stone door standing at the far end of the chamber.","\"There it is.\"","Noah grinned.","\"That looks important.\"","Surprisingly, this door was also partially open. The two exchanged glances before stepping through.","The room beyond was shrouded in darkness.","Mary raised the torch higher. The light swept across the chamber.","She watched the walls, floor, ceiling. There was nothing special.","Then suddenly the torchlight landed upon something massive.","Both froze at what they just saw.","Their eyes widened.","\"Th-That’s...\"","Noah stared in fascination.","A gigantic stone statue stood before them. It towered nearly twenty meters high.","The figure depicted a woman. Yet calling her merely a woman felt wrong.","She looked divine.","She looked otherworldly with beautiful carving that put life into her.","A long stone robe flowed around her body like cascading water. Intricate celestial patterns had been carved into the fabric, depicting stars, moons, and constellations.","A veil covered her face. Even that veil was carved by stone. Even though her features remained hidden, an overwhelming sense of beauty and majesty radiated from the statue.","It felt impossible to look away.","Both of her hands were extended forward. Resting gently upon her joined palms was a large stone sphere. At first glance it appeared ordinary.","Then Mary narrowed her eyes.","She stepped closer as Noah walked with her.","It felt like her observation ability activated instinctively. The details became clearer.","Then realization struck her.","\"Noah...\"","\"What?\"","\"That’s not a sphere.\"","She pointed at it.","\"It’s the moon.\"","Noah blinked.","\"The moon?\"","He pulled his arm from her shoulder and stepped closer and studied it carefully. Now that Mary had mentioned it, the surface truly resembled the moon.","The light of torch was landed on the sphere. There were countless craters and circular patterns on it.","Ancient carvings resembling lunar phases.","Slowly Noah nodded. \"...You’re right.\"","Mary stared at the statue.","\"A woman holding the moon...\"","Her voice carried disbelief.","Noah folded his arms.","\"Then she must be a Moon Goddess.\" He immediately came to a conclusion.","Mary immediately turned toward him.","\"What?\"","\"Why are you surprised?\" He asked, wondering why she was shocked.","\"There has never been a Moon Goddess in recorded history.\"","Noah looked back toward the statue. The longer he stared at it, the stranger he felt. A cold sensation crawled across his skin.","An inexplicable pressure lingered in the air.","It was not hostile nor it was friendly.","But Noah felt one thing that was dangerous, as though the statue was silently watching them.","Mary suddenly pointed behind it. \"Noah.\"","\"What now?\" Her voiced pulled out Noah from his focus.","\"I think there’s another room.\" She spoked while pointing there.","Noah frowned. \"What?\"","Mary moved to the side and shone the torch behind the enormous statue.","He followed her, dragging his weak trembling body. There, hidden completely from the entrance, was another stone doorway.","Noah’s eyes widened.","\"Wow.\"","He looked at her with genuine admiration. \"Your observation ability is incredible.\"","Mary smiled shyly. \"It’s nothing special.\"","\"It definitely is.\"","Noah’s curiosity immediately doubled.","\"Alright.\"","He pointed toward the hidden doorway.","\"Let’s see what’s behind it.\"","Together they stepped past the mysterious statue.","Leaving behind the silent Moon Goddess.","And entered the hidden chamber concealed beyond her gaze.","---","[A/N: Sorry for one Chapter. Also the arc will soon come to end. Sighed. I really want to write lots of romance Chapters for this novel as well. Well I have to wait for few hundred more Chapters. Since I am slow on romance side. Also do you guys like milfs? My next novel will have milf as female lead...keke just joking. Also In kofi acc, each time i reach 20$ donation mark, I will do 3 bonus Chapters! 2 for one novel and 1 for another. Depends on you guys!!]"]},{"number":194,"title":"Chapter 194: A Mysterious Experience","paragraphs":["The hidden doorway led into a narrow stone passage.","Unlike the grand corridors they had explored earlier, this one was barely wide enough for two people to walk side by side.","The walls felt rough and unfinished, as though this section had been carved directly through solid rock instead of being constructed by skilled craftsmen.","Their footsteps echoed softly through the confined tunnel.","Tap.","Tap.","Tap.","The air had grown noticeably colder.","Neither of them spoke. Only the flickering torchlight danced across the ancient walls as they continued deeper into the unknown.","After walking for nearly a minute, the passage suddenly widened.","Both of them stepped out of the narrow corridor and stopped instinctively. Before them stretched another underground chamber.","This one was even larger than the previous hall. The ceiling rose so high that the torchlight couldn’t reach it. Countless stone pillars stood throughout the chamber like silent guardians, disappearing into darkness above.","The silence was overwhelming. It almost felt alive.","Mary slowly looked around before taking a deep breath. \"This hall is enormous.\"","\"It really is...\" Noah’s eyes swept across the vast chamber.","Even in the dim torchlight, he could tell this room was far larger than the hall containing the mysterious Moon Goddess.","Mary gently handed him the torch.","\"You take this.\"","Noah accepted it. \"What about you?\"","A small flame suddenly ignited above Mary’s palm. The orange fire hovered steadily without burning her skin, illuminating her surroundings.","\"I’ll use this.\"","The dancing flame cast warm light across her face. \"You check that side,\" she said while pointing toward the far end of the chamber.","\"I’ll search this half.\"","Noah nodded. \"Alright.\"","Normally, splitting up inside an unknown ruin would have been a terrible idea. But the chamber was so vast that searching together would only waste time.","Besides, they could still see each other from where they stood.","\"Be careful,\" Mary reminded him.","\"You too.\"","Supporting himself with a stick made up of ice, Noah slowly dragged his exhausted body across the stone floor.","Each step sent a dull ache through his muscles.","The battle against Xavier had pushed him beyond his limits. Even after drinking recovery potions and receiving Mary’s healing magic, his body still protested with every movement.","Yet curiosity continued driving him forward. The chamber was strangely empty. Here there was no statues. There were no inscriptions. Nor there any treasure.","Only endless silence. His footsteps echoed faintly throughout the massive hall.","Tap.","Tap.","Tap.","After walking for some distance, something unusual caught his attention.","Noah stopped. \"...Hm?\"","The wall ahead looked. It wasn’t made from stone. He frowned. Slowly, he approached. The torchlight illuminated the surface.","His eyes widened slightly. \"It... isn’t stone.\"","The entire wall was made of an enormous sheet of black crystal.","’Is it crystal? Glass?","It stretched from one end of the chamber to the other, perfectly smooth and seamless. Its surface was so dark that it resembled an endless night sky.","Noah stepped closer. The torchlight should have reflected brightly against it.","Instead, only a faint, dull glow appeared.","Almost as though the darkness itself was swallowing the light.","\"...Strange.\"","He cautiously extended a hand. His fingertips touched the surface. A freezing sensation spread through his palm.","It wasn’t ordinary cold. It felt different, even for someone like him who uses ice element. This felt really weird.","As if the darkness beyond the glass had been sleeping for countless centuries.","Noah slowly slid his hand across the surface while walking alongside it. The glass remained perfectly smooth.","There were no cracks on it. The surface was smooth and plain.","\"What is this...?\"","His blue eyes narrowed. Something about the wall felt wrong. It wasn’t merely reflective. It almost didn’t feel like a wall at all.","Rather, it felt like a window that was looking into somewhere else. As if there was another chamber on other side. Another world existed there.","Or perhaps somewhere that shouldn’t exist.","That thought alone sent an inexplicable chill crawling down his spine. His grip on the torch tightened.","He raised it higher. The light of his torch barely illuminated the dark surface. Then Noah froze. His breathing stopped.","Far beyond the glass. At least ten meters inside, someone was standing there. It was silhouette that was perfectly still.","A human-shaped figure. It wasn’t reflected beside him. It wasn’t behind him. It was Inside the glass.","Noah’s pupils contracted. His heartbeat suddenly quickened.","Thump.","Thump.","Thump.","The torch trembled slightly in his hand. His mouth had gone completely dry.","He swallowed hard. The figure never moved.","It simply stood there watching him.","Noah unconsciously leaned closer. His blue eyes strained to pierce the unnatural darkness. Slowly more details emerged.","It looked as though another enormous corridor existed beyond the black glass. Then another transparent barrier.","And behind that another distant chamber. Inside that chamber, the humanoid figure remained motionless. Then it moved. It’s hand touched the surface of glass and tried to look at other side.","Its features were impossible to distinguish. Only its outline could be seen.","It was keenly watching Noah.","Every instinct in Noah’s body screamed that something was terribly wrong. A cold sweat trickled down his neck.","His breathing became shallow. He couldn’t look away.","The longer he stared. The more it felt as though the figure was staring back.","\"Noah!\"","Mary’s voice suddenly echoed across the hall.","He flinched violently. His heart nearly leaped out of his chest.","He spun around.","Mary was jogging toward him, concern clearly visible on her face.","\"Noah?\"","She stopped a few steps away.","\"What happened?\"","Only then did Noah realize how heavily he was breathing. His chest rose and fell rapidly. His forehead was covered in cold sweat.","His hand holding the torch trembled slightly. He immediately turned back toward the black glass.","\"There!\"","He pointed at it.","\"Look!\"","Mary frowned before following his gaze.","\"...Where?\"","\"There was someone inside!\"","Noah stepped closer again.","\"I saw someone standing behind this glass.\"","Mary walked over and examined the surface carefully. The black wall reflected only the dim torchlight. There was nothing else. There was no distant corridor.","No mysterious chamber that he spoke about. There was no humanoid silhouette. Only Noah’s own reflection stared back at him.","He frowned deeply.","\"...Impossible. I definitely saw someone.\"","Mary looked from the glass to Noah. Then back again. After several long seconds, she gently sighed.","\"Noah... I think you’re simply exhausted. You pushed yourself far beyond your limits. You’ve lost a lot of blood. It’s possible you imagined it.\"","Noah remained silent. His eyes stayed fixed on the glass. His reflection stared back at him.","There was nothing more.","\"...Maybe...\"","Even as he said those words... He didn’t believe them. Because what he had seen. And it had felt far too real.","Mary gently touched his shoulder.","\"Come on. We should rest. If this place is truly important, we can continue exploring after you’ve recovered.\"","Noah remained motionless for several more seconds.","Finally he nodded.","\"...Alright.\"","The two of them slowly walked away from the mysterious black wall. Their footsteps gradually disappeared into the darkness.","Silence returned to the chamber once again.","The two of them slowly retraced their steps. Neither Noah nor Mary spoke.","The eerie silence of the ancient ruin pressed heavily upon them, broken only by the soft echoes of their footsteps.","Mary continued supporting Noah as they made their way back through the enormous hall. The torch in Noah’s hand cast long, flickering shadows across the ancient pillars.","Noah’s body ached with every step.","His muscles screamed in protest, and the deep wound across his chest throbbed despite the healing magic Mary had used earlier.","’I really pushed myself too far. ’ The battle against Xavier had drained nearly everything he had. His mana was almost exhausted. His body was barely holding together.","Still, he forced himself to remain alert.","After what he had witnessed beyond that strange black glass, he no longer believed this ruin was merely an abandoned temple.","It was something that perhaps should never have been disturbed.","Soon, the narrow passage leading back toward the Moon Goddess’ chamber came into view. They stepped through it cautiously. Then went in front of statue.","Then both of them froze. The torchlight illuminated two figures standing motionlessly at the entrance.","Neither of them had been there before.","One possessed neatly combed burgundy hair and calm amber eyes. He looked to be in his late twenties and wore dark leather armor beneath a long black cloak.","Beside him stood a broad-shouldered man with messy black hair and a thick beard. He carried a heavy sword resting casually against his shoulder.","Neither looked surprised.","They looked as though they had been waiting. The burgundy-haired man smiled faintly.","\"So... In the end, someone really did find this place.\"","Silence filled the corridor.","Noah’s eyes narrowed immediately. His instincts screamed that these two weren’t ordinary explorers.","They were dangerous.","Without saying a word, Noah step forward.","Mary also reacted instantly. She raised her wand defensively while taking a defensive stance.","\"Who are you two?\"","Her voice echoed through the stone corridor. The two men exchanged amused glances.","Then both chuckled. The burgundy-haired man placed a hand over his chest and bowed slightly as though introducing himself at a formal gathering.","\"My name is Boris.\"","He gestured toward the bearded man beside him.","\"And this grumpy fellow is Albert.\"","Albert snorted.","\"I hate introductions.\"","Boris ignored him and continued smiling.","\"We came here on a mission.\"","His expression gradually turned cold.","\"And unfortunately...You two also came here.\"","His amber eyes settled on Noah. \"That means we can’t allow either of you to leave this place alive.\"","Mary’s grip around her wand tightened.","\"What do you mean?\"","Boris sighed dramatically.","\"It means... We’re going to kill both of you.\"","The atmosphere instantly became suffocating.","Noah quietly shifted his footing. His breathing remained uneven, but his gaze never left the two men.","His exhausted body begged him to retreat. His instincts told him to run. But there was nowhere to run.","The narrow corridor behind them offered no escape. The only exit was blocked by the two strangers.","\"Tch...\"","Noah clicked his tongue softly. ’Of all the times...’","Boris smiled.","\"It seems you’re ready.\""]},{"number":195,"title":"Chapter 195: The Battle Was Finally Over?","paragraphs":["Clang!","Noah barely managed to block Boris’ next strike. The impact numbed both of his arms. His feet slid backward across the ancient stone floor, leaving shallow marks behind.","\"Ghk...\"","His chest burned with pain.","Every clash reopened the wounds that had only begun to heal.","Boris wore a faint smile.","\"You’ve reached your limit.\"","His twin daggers flashed once more.","Clang!","Clang!","Clang!","The attacks flowed one after another without pause. Each strike was heavier than the last.","To Noah, it felt as though massive boulders were crashing against his sword. His exhausted body could barely keep up.","On the other side of the corridor, Mary was having no easier time. Another orange magic circle formed before her.","[Fire Lance.]","Three blazing spears shot toward Albert.","Whoosh!","Whoosh!","Whoosh!","Albert snorted.","Mana surged around his greatsword. He swung the sword at incoming attacks.","BOOM!!","The fire lances exploded before reaching him. The blast filled the corridor with smoke and scorching heat.","Albert continued charging through the explosion as though it had never happened. His enormous sword came crashing downward.","Mary hastily conjured a barrier.","Crack!","The translucent shield shattered instantly. The remaining force threw her backward.","Bang!","She slammed against the stone wall before stumbling back onto her feet.","\"Cough...!\"","Blood trickled from the corner of her lips.","Noah saw everything from the corner of his eye. His expression darkened.","’Dammit...’","They couldn’t win. Not in his current condition. He had exhausted nearly all of his mana fighting Xavier. His muscles were torn. His body had reached its limit.","Mary had also spent a considerable amount of mana healing him and supporting him throughout the earlier battles.","Continuing this fight would only get them killed.","Boris noticed the hesitation in Noah’s eyes.","\"You’ve realized it too. There was never any chance.\"","His daggers danced forward again.","Clang!","Clang!","Clang!","Noah blocked desperately, but every impact pushed him farther back.","\"Mary!\"","He shouted without taking his eyes off Boris.","\"We’re running!\"","Mary immediately understood. She didn’t question him for even a second.","\"Got it!\"","She thrust her wand toward Albert. A brilliant crimson magic circle expanded before her.","[Flame Burst]","Boom!!","A violent explosion of fire erupted between them. The corridor disappeared beneath flames and thick smoke.","Albert instinctively raised an arm to shield his face.","\"Tch!\"","At the same moment, Noah unleashed several ice spikes from the ground beneath Boris.","Crack!","Crack!","Crack!","Sharp pillars of ice erupted upward. Boris leaped backward. The attack hadn’t injured him. But it had bought them exactly what they needed.","\"Now!\"","Noah grabbed Mary’s wrist. The two of them spun around and sprinted deeper into the ruins. Their footsteps echoed frantically through the ancient corridor.","Tap!","Tap!","Tap!","They burst into the enormous hall containing the Moon Goddess statue. Towering pillars rushed past them.","The flickering torch still lay abandoned near the entrance, its light growing fainter behind them.","Noah’s breathing became ragged. Every stride sent agonizing pain through his battered body. His vision blurred for a moment.","Still he forced himself to keep moving.","’Just... a little farther...’","Mary stayed beside him despite being exhausted herself.","\"Noah!\"","\"I’m fine!\"","He lied through gritted teeth. Blood slowly dripped from beneath his academy battle gear. His healing wounds had opened once again.","Boom!","The smoke exploded apart. Boris and Albert emerged from it at terrifying speed.","\"They’re escaping!\"","Albert roared.","\"Don’t let them leave this place!\"","Both men accelerated. Their footsteps thundered across the stone floor as they chased after the fleeing students.","The distance between them rapidly shrank.","\"They’re catching up!\" Mary shouted.","\"I know!\"","Noah glanced ahead.","The long staircase leading toward the upper passages came into view.","\"There!\"","They immediately changed direction and rushed toward it.","Step!","Step!","Step!","The ancient stairs stretched upward into darkness. Noah gritted his teeth and forced his aching legs to move faster.","Every muscle in his body screamed in protest. His lungs burned. His vision swam. Yet he refused to stop.","Behind them, Boris smiled coldly. \"They won’t get far.\"","Albert tightened his grip on his massive sword.","\"We’ll finish them before they reach the surface.\"","The chase through the ancient ruin had only just begun.","---","Back to Damien and the others.","Damien remained standing, his body bathed in a faint golden glow.","Cuts and bruises covered him from head to toe. Blood dripped steadily from several wounds, soaking parts of his academy battle gear. Even so, he refused to fall.","Several meters ahead, Daniel lay motionless on the forest floor.","The demon’s body was riddled with deep sword wounds, his lifeless eyes staring blankly toward the darkening sky.","Beside Damien stood Lyria, breathing heavily. Her chest rose and fell rapidly as she leaned on her golden spear for support.","\"We... we did it...\"","Damien let out a weary breath and nodded.","\"...Yeah.\"","The golden aura surrounding him slowly faded. The pressure he had been suppressing all this time finally caught up to him.","His knees buckled.","Thud.","Damien collapsed onto one knee before falling completely onto the ground. The last traces of golden light vanished from his body.","\"Damien!\"","Lyria hurried to his side and knelt beside him.","The forest had become almost completely dark, with only the faint crimson glow of the evening sky filtering through the dense canopy overhead.","Without wasting a moment, she raised her hand. A soft golden-white magic circle formed beneath Damien.","Warm healing light spread across his battered body, slowly closing the smaller wounds while easing the pain in his muscles.","As she examined him, her eyes widened slightly.","\"...He broke through.\"","A faint smile appeared on her face.","\"He reached the Condensed Core Realm... Low Rank.\"","Despite being unconscious from exhaustion, Damien had advanced during the life-and-death battle.","Lyria let out a relieved sigh.","\"...What a monster.\"","---","Meanwhile...","On the other side of the forest...","The battle between Botis and the three students had reached its final stage. Kaelan, Ken, and Arisha stood several meters apart, surrounding the demon from three different directions.","All three were exhausted.","Kaelan was in the worst condition.","Blood flowed continuously from multiple wounds across his body, and his breathing had become uneven. Even holding his twin daggers had become difficult.","Ken wasn’t much better.","His clothes were torn in several places, and numerous cuts covered his arms and shoulders. Fresh blood dripped steadily from the tip of his sword.","Arisha’s mana had nearly been depleted.","Sweat covered her forehead as she held her wand tightly. The blue crystal embedded at its tip glowed faintly, showing just how little mana she had left.","Across from them Botis still stood.","Although the demon remained imposing, he was far from uninjured.","Deep cuts crossed both of his arms. One of Arisha’s wind arrows had pierced completely through his thigh. A long diagonal slash stretched across his chest, staining his clothes crimson.","Blood continued to drip onto the forest floor.","Yet despite everything...He remained standing tall.","His crimson eyes swept across the three students with undisguised irritation. His grip around the spear tightened.","\"You brats...\"","His voice was cold and filled with killing intent.","\"...You’re far more persistent than I expected.\"","He clicked his tongue. A Condensed Core Realm warrior like himself had spent so much time fighting three academy students.","Worse, his primary target was still alive.","It was humiliating.","Botis slowly lowered his stance. Dark orange flames began swirling around his spear once again.","The surrounding air distorted from the intense heat.","\"I’m done playing.\"","His mana surged violently.","\"This time...\"","\"...Kaelan dies.\"","The terrifying pressure swept across the battlefield.","Kaelan tightened his grip on both daggers. Despite his battered body, he stepped forward without hesitation.","Ken silently moved beside him, his sword raised.","Arisha pointed her wand toward Botis.","The three prepared themselves for one final clash.","Botis bent his knees.","The ground beneath his feet cracked. Just as he was about to launch himself forward—A black magic circle silently appeared beneath him.","Botis frowned.","\"...What?\"","Dark matter erupted from the circle like liquid shadows. It wrapped around his legs before rapidly climbing over the rest of his body.","\"What is this?!\"","He struggled violently, attempting to tear free. The dark substance only tightened further. Within seconds, it completely engulfed him.","His furious voice abruptly disappeared. Silence returned to the battlefield.","A calm, slightly tired voice echoed from among the trees.","\"...Seems I’m late again.\"","The students immediately turned toward the source. A familiar figure stepped out from the darkness.","The dark magic restraining Botis was clearly under her control.","\"Instructor Morgana!\"","Relief instantly filled Arisha’s face. She nearly dropped her wand.","Kaelan finally let out the breath he had been holding.","His tense shoulders relaxed.","\"...We made it.\"","His legs finally gave out.","Thud.","He dropped onto the ground, breathing heavily. He was alive and safe. At one point he really thought that he was going to die.","Ken also lowered his sword. The tension that had gripped his body slowly disappeared.","The battle was finally over."]},{"number":196,"title":"Chapter 196: The Cost Of Survival","paragraphs":["Both Noah and Mary sprinted up the ancient stone staircase as though their lives depended on it. Because they did. Behind them, the two mysterious men pursued relentlessly.","They weren’t demons like Xavier. They were humans. That only made Noah even more confused.","’Who are they? Why are they here? Why are they trying to kill us?’","He couldn’t understand any of it.","’These two probably have nothing to do with the demons... But damn it! Why do I keep running into one disaster after another?’","Noah silently cursed his luck.","Wissshhh!!","Several arrows made entirely of compressed water shot toward them from behind.","\"Mary! Down!\"","Without hesitation, both of them threw themselves down. The water arrows whistled over their heads before crashing into the stone ceiling above the staircase.","BOOOM!!","Chunks of stone exploded outward.","\"Noah! Run!\"","Mary was already back on her feet.","Noah forced his exhausted body to move and followed her.","THUD!","CRASH!!","Massive fragments of broken rock crashed onto the staircase behind them, partially blocking the path.","The collapse slowed Boris and Albert for a moment.","Boris clicked his tongue.","\"Albert! Use your brain when you attack! This passage isn’t wide enough. If you keep using large-scale spells, you’ll bring the whole place down!\"","Albert grunted.","\"...Yeah. Got it.\"","Taking advantage of the delay, Noah and Mary continued running.","Soon, the staircase finally ended.","The narrow passage leading toward the surface came into view. Without slowing down, they rushed into it.","\"Fuu... Haa...\"","Noah gasped heavily.","Every breath burned his lungs. His entire body screamed at him to stop. His muscles were trembling. His mana was nearly exhausted.","Yet he couldn’t afford to slow down.","Mary glanced at him with obvious worry. \"Noah! Hang in there! We’re almost out!\"","\"...Yeah.\"","His blue eyes remained fixed on the faint light at the end of the tunnel.","Stomp.","Stomp.","Stomp.","’Just a little farther... Only a few more meters... We can make it...’","Suddenly, a translucent notification appeared before Noah’s eyes.","[A Reward is Available.]","[Would you like to claim it?]","Noah ignored it immediately.","’Not now. What if the reward causes another painful evolution? I can’t risk that while we’re running.’","Behind them, Boris and Albert were rapidly closing the distance.","\"You two aren’t getting away!\"","Noah and Mary burst through the massive metal doorway and entered the earthen tunnel that led back to the surface.","At that exact moment, Albert extended his hand. A gigantic sphere of compressed water, nearly the size of a human body, condensed before him.","The amount of mana inside it was terrifying. It shot forward like a cannonball.","Mary sensed the danger first.","\"Noah!\"","She threw herself at him without hesitation. Both of them tumbled aside. The enormous water sphere flew past the spot where they had been standing only a heartbeat earlier.","BOOOOOOMMMM!!!","The explosion shook the entire underground tunnel. The blast pulverized the surrounding earth. Cracks spread across the ceiling like a spider’s web. Dust and broken stone erupted in every direction.","Even though Noah and Mary had avoided a direct hit, the shockwave still slammed into them. Their bodies were hurled through the air before crashing violently against the earthen wall.","BANG!!","Noah felt every bone in his body rattle. Behind the thick cloud of dust, Boris cursed.","\"Where did they go?!\"","\"The tunnel’s collapsing!\"","Mary groaned as she pushed herself to her feet. Her body ached, but she ignored the pain.","\"Noah!\"","She rushed toward him.","Noah was in far worse condition. Blood stained his clothes. His breathing had become ragged.","His vision blurred every few seconds. \"Come on!\"","Mary wrapped one of his arms around her shoulders and helped him stand.","\"Damn it...\"","Noah gritted his teeth.","\"My body won’t move...\"","\"You have to!\"","Mary practically dragged him forward.","\"We’re almost outside!\"","Supporting most of his weight, she hurried toward the exit. Ahead of them, the tunnel sloped upward.","Only one last climb remained before they could escape.","BOOM!!","Another spell exploded.","BOOM!!","Albert continued firing powerful water spells into the tunnel. Each explosion made the underground passage tremble violently.","Large cracks spread across the ceiling. Chunks of earth continuously fell around them.","\"We’re almost there, Noah!\"","Hope appeared in Mary’s eyes. Only a few more steps, just a little more steps they needed.","They were now near hole which was upward. Dim moonlight came from it.","But just then Albert’s figure suddenly blurred. Using reinforcement magic, he burst forward with explosive speed.","In an instant, he closed the remaining distance. His massive greatsword thrust forward like a spear. Its target was Noah’s back.","Noah sensed the killing intent. His instincts reacted immediately.","’Ice Wall! form it.’","He tried to gather mana. A sharp pain exploded inside his mana core. Nothing happened. His mana had been completely depleted from last use he did while running.","There wasn’t enough left to create even a thin layer of ice. Noah’s eyes widened.","’No...!’","SLASH!!","The sound of flesh being pierced echoed through the tunnel. Hot blood splashed across Noah’s back.","But he felt no pain. Confused, he slowly turned around. His pupils shrank. \"Ma... Mary...?\"","Mary was standing directly behind him. Albert’s massive sword had pierced straight through her back before emerging from her chest.","Bright crimson blood flowed continuously from the wound.","\"Cough...\"","She coughed up another mouthful of blood. The droplets splattered across Noah’s chest. Time seemed to stop. Noah stared at her blankly. His mind refused to accept what he was seeing.","\"Mary...!\"","His voice trembled. Mary slowly raised both trembling hands. Instead of touching her own wound...","She gently placed them against Noah’s chest. Noah was bend forward. Since he was to tired.","\"N-Noah...\"","Before he could say another word, a powerful surge of mana erupted from her body.","BOOOOM!!","A tremendous gust of compressed wind exploded outward. It perfectly send him in direction of hole.","\"Arghhh!\"","Noah was launched upward with overwhelming force. His body shot through the vertical tunnel leading to the surface like an arrow released from a bow. he couldn’t believe how she was able to do it. This was very weird.","THUD!!","He crashed onto the grassy ground outside. His body rolled several times before coming to a stop. Everything hurt, yet he ignored it.","\"Mary...!\"","He desperately tried to crawl back toward the entrance.","RUMBLE!!","The ground shook violently. The entire underground tunnel finally gave way. With a deafening roar, the earth collapsed inward.","The entrance caved in completely. Tons of rock and soil buried the passage beneath them in an instant.","\"No...!\"","Noah reached out desperately.","\"Mary!!\"","The collapsing ground swallowed part of his body as well. His legs became trapped beneath the loose earth.","Blood continued flowing from countless wounds. His vision blurred. The world around him gradually faded into darkness.","Still reaching toward the buried entrance. Noah finally lost consciousness.","The gentle moon light covered his unconscious body."]},{"number":197,"title":"Chapter 197: The Beginning of a New Fate","paragraphs":["Noah’s eyelids twitched faintly before slowly opening.","At first, everything was blurry. His thoughts were sluggish, as though his mind had been submerged beneath an endless ocean.","The excruciating pain that had tormented him only moments ago had vanished completely, disappearing as if it had never existed.","’Where am I...? What happened...?’","He struggled to gather his memories. Then they came rushing back.","The underground passage where he was running alongside Mary.","’Mary...’","His eyes widened.","\"Ma... Mary!\"","He abruptly tried to sit up. His vision finally began to clear.","What greeted him wasn’t the forest. Nor was it the underground ruin. Instead, beneath him stretched an endless expanse of rough gray ground, barren and lifeless.","It resembled weathered stone, scarred by countless cracks and untouched by any sign of life.","There was no trees, no wind nor any sound. There was only silence.","\"...What?\"","Noah slowly pushed himself to his feet. His eyes wandered across the desolate landscape before instinctively lifting toward the sky. His breath caught.","Above him stretched a sea of stars unlike anything he had ever witnessed. Countless brilliant stars glittered across the endless darkness.","Some shone silver. Others glowed with hues of crimson, sapphire, emerald, and violet.","Nebulas painted distant stretches of space with faint ribbons of celestial light, giving the heavens an almost dreamlike beauty.","It was as though he were standing at the very edge of the universe itself.","\"...Where am I?\"","His voice echoed softly before disappearing into the endless silence.","Then as he slowly turned around. His entire body froze.","His pupils contracted. Far away in the darkness hung an enormous celestial sphere. A breathtaking planet floated silently through space.","Its vast oceans shimmered with deep sapphire blue, while emerald-green continents stretched across its surface like precious jewels.","Massive swirls of white clouds drifted gracefully around the world.","A faint golden glow outlined its horizon, making the entire planet appear almost divine. It was unimaginably beautiful.","Noah stared blankly.","\"T-That’s...\"","His voice trembled.","\"...Earth?\"","He immediately shook his head. \"No...\"","His eyes widened even further. \"...Not Earth. It... it’s Terranis.\"","The world where he had been transmigrated. The very planet on which he now lived.","He was looking at it from space. An impossible sight. His breathing became uneven.","’How...? How am I here on the moon? Why can I breathe? Am I... dead?’","His mind descended into complete confusion.","Crack.","A strange sound echoed through the silent void.","Noah’s body stiffened.","Slowly he turned around. Nearly ten meters behind him, the space itself cracked. A thin fracture appeared in empty air.","Like shattered glass. The crack spread wider.","Crack.","Crack.","The fracture continued expanding until it stood more than two meters tall.","Beyond it there was nothing. There was only endless darkness.","Not even starlight could enter that abyss. Noah unconsciously swallowed.","\"What...\"","He couldn’t understand what he was witnessing.","A foot stepped out from the darkness. It touched the gray ground soundlessly. Another followed. A tall figure slowly emerged from the fractured space.","The instant Noah saw her. His entire body became rigid. A chilling sensation ran down his spine.","His breathing stopped.","She wore flowing robes of pure lunar white that draped elegantly over her tall, slender figure. The fabric seemed almost unreal, shimmering faintly like moonlight dancing across calm water.","A long white veil covered her head and concealed everything above her lips. Only her pale chin remained visible beneath it.","Several strands of hair escaped from beneath the veil. They were the color of fresh blood red. While near the roots, gradually fading into a soft light lunar-blue at their ends, glowing faintly beneath the countless stars.","Her skin was unnaturally pale. Not the pale complexion of an ordinary woman. It was as though no blood had ever flowed beneath it.","She stood nearly two meters tall. She was graceful, elegant and perfect.","Yet what stole Noah’s breath wasn’t her appearance. He couldn’t see her face since she wore a veil.","It was her presence. It wasn’t something that could be described with words. She didn’t simply look powerful.","She felt divine and otherworldly. Like a being who existed far beyond mortal understanding. Standing before her made Noah feel smaller than an ant before the heavens.","It wasn’t merely fear. It was instinct. Every fiber of his being screamed that this existence stood at a level infinitely above him.","If she wished she could erase him with nothing more than a thought.","’Is she...The Moon Goddess...?’","His mind flashed back to the enormous statue hidden within the ancient temple.","’It’s her... She’s definitely the Moon Goddess...’","Cold sweat formed across his forehead. His thoughts spiraled wildly.","’Why am I here? Did she summon me? Was she the one who brought me into this world? Or did she discover that I’m not the original Noah? ...Is she going to kill me?’","He didn’t know. He couldn’t understand anything.","The mysterious goddess continued walking toward him. Her footsteps made no sound. Yet each step carried a pressure that felt heavier than mountains.","Noah wanted to retreat. He wanted to move. But his body refused.","It was as though space itself had imprisoned him. His muscles wouldn’t obey. His voice wouldn’t come out.","Soon she stood directly before him, towering over him.","He still couldn’t see her face beneath the veil. Silence stretched between them.","She simply observed him.","Slowly she raised her right hand. Her movements were graceful beyond description.","Her pale fingers stopped inches from Noah’s forehead. Only her index finger extended.","Tap.","The fingertip touched the center of his forehead.","Instantly an unbearable coldness spread through his body. It wasn’t ordinary cold. It felt as though winter itself had entered his bloodstream.","His blood froze. His bones froze. His muscles froze. Even his soul seemed to freeze.","Noah desperately tried to move. Nothing happened. His body no longer belonged to him. His eyes widened in terror.","’Am...Am I going to die...?’","He looked up at the silent goddess.","She never spoke. She simply watched. The freezing sensation intensified. Ice crystals slowly spread across his fingertips.","Then it moved to his hands, his arms, his chest.","Frost climbed across his neck before reaching his cheeks. His eyelashes froze. His vision gradually became obscured by a layer of crystalline ice.","Finally his entire body became a flawless statue of transparent blue ice.","Only his eyes remained fixed upon the silent goddess standing before him beneath the endless sea of stars.","Darkness slowly swallowed his vision. The last thing Noah saw was the mysterious veiled goddess silently gazing at him.","Crack.","His frozen body shattered into countless glittering fragments of ice. The crystalline shards drifted silently into the darkness. Until nothing remained.","---","[End Of The Volume 1: The Beginning of a New Fate ]"]},{"number":198,"title":"Chapter 198: Reward","paragraphs":["The first thing Noah saw when he opened his eyes was a familiar white ceiling.","He blinked several times, his vision gradually clearing. His breathing remained slow and steady as the lingering haze of unconsciousness faded away.","\"...Where...?\"","He turned his head slightly.","The room was spacious and spotless. Rows of neatly arranged beds stretched across the infirmary, separated by white curtains. The faint scent of medicinal herbs mixed with disinfectant filled the air.","The Academy infirmary.","A quiet sigh escaped his lips. \"So... I survived...\"","As he attempted to sit up, a soft female voice interrupted him. \"Oh? You’re finally awake.\"","A woman wearing a white lab coat approached his bedside. She appeared to be in her early thirties, her gentle eyes carrying the calm composure of an experienced healer.","She placed two fingers on his wrist before channeling a thread of mana through his body to examine his condition.","After a few moments, she nodded in satisfaction. \"Your pulse is stable.\"","She looked into his eyes.","\"How are you feeling? Any dizziness? Difficulty breathing? Pain anywhere?\"","Noah slowly shook his head.","\"...I’m fine. Just feeling weak.\"","\"That’s good.\"","She smiled faintly before saying,","\"You’ve been unconscious for two whole days.\"","Noah blinked in surprise.","\"...Two days?\"","He hadn’t expected that. He only remembered escaping the underground passage.","Mary.","The healer adjusted the blanket covering him.","\"Your injuries were severe. You had exhausted nearly all of your mana, suffered extensive muscle damage, internal injuries, and mana channel fatigue. Frankly, it’s surprising you recovered this quickly.\"","Noah remained silent.","The healer stood up. \"You should continue resting. If everything remains stable, you’ll probably be discharged this evening.\"","\"...Okay.\"","She turned to leave.","\"Wait.\"","The healer stopped and looked back.","Noah’s expression became tense. \"What happened to Mary?\"","His voice had become noticeably quieter. He was really worried about her. he didn’t remember what happened after he was thrown out of the hole.","\"The student who was with me. Is she alright? Is she safe? And what about the exam? What happened to the demons that attacked us? What about Damien... Kaelan... everyone else?\"","The questions poured out one after another. His breathing unconsciously became faster.","The healer noticed the panic growing in his expression.","She gently raised one hand. \"Calm down. Your body still needs rest.\"","She gently said, \"I can’t answer those questions.\"","She gave him a reassuring smile. \"I’ll inform your head instructor that you’ve regained consciousness. She will come her and explain everything herself.\"","Noah slowly lowered his gaze.","\"...Alright.\"","The healer quietly walked out of the room, closing the door behind her. Silence filled the infirmary once again.","Noah leaned back against the pillow. Mary’s final moments replayed vividly inside his mind.","Her body, the massive sword piercing through her chest.","The blood that belong to Mary staining his clothes. Her trembling hands reaching toward him.","Her desperate smile.","\"...Noah...\"","He slowly covered his eyes with his forearm. His teeth clenched tightly. An unbearable ache spread through his chest. He already knew what had most likely happened.","Since the first day he came to this world, Noah felt so much pain. Because of someone’s death.","Somewhere deep inside. He still wished he was wrong. After several long moments, he lowered his arm.","His eyes had become slightly red, moisture gathering at their corners.","Just then a familiar translucent screen appeared before him.","[A reward is available.]","[Would you like to claim it?]","[ YES ]","Noah stared at it quietly. Normally, he would have accepted it immediately.","He would have wondered what new ability or reward awaited him.","But today he felt almost nothing. After a long silence, he slowly raised his hand. His movements were sluggish.","His fingertip touched the floating [YES] button.","The screen dissolved into countless particles before reforming.","A mechanical female voice echoed inside his mind.","[Congratulations, Extra!]","[You have successfully survived the Fourth Act of Chapter I — First Semester Exam: Hunting for Kaelan.]","[First Chapter of The Game ’Odyssey Of Eternal Gods’ War’, The Beginning of The New Fate has ended. Congratulations!]","[Despite encountering multiple hostile demons during the examination, you survived the battle, eliminated enemy targets, protected Kaelan, and discovered the hidden underground Temple of the Moon Goddess.]","[Reward Granted:]","[Passive Ability Acquired — Heart of Absolute Frost]","[Complete immunity to ice and cold-based damage. Significantly increases the power of all Ice-element spells and techniques. Allows survival in environments approaching Absolute Zero.]","Another notification appeared almost immediately.","[Congratulations!]","[Your bloodline has responded to recent events.]","[Active Bloodline Ability Awakened.]","The floating blue windows remained suspended for several seconds.","Then they quietly dissolved into countless tiny particles before disappearing completely, leaving behind nothing except the silent atmosphere of the infirmary.","Noah stared blankly at the empty space.","He was surprised. Not by the rewards themselves but by the mention of the Moon Goddess.","\"So... it wasn’t an illusion...\"","He unconsciously touched his forehead. He could still remember that freezing fingertip.","That divine presence. That overwhelming pressure. The mysterious woman.","The statue beneath the ruins. The frozen world beneath the stars.","Were they truly connected? Before he could think further.","The sound of door opening came.","The handle slowly turned. The door opened. A tall woman entered the room.","Her long sky-blue hair flowed elegantly behind her, reaching almost to her waist. Today she didn’t tie them in bun.","Amethyst-colored eyes observed him calmly.","Her beautiful face remained expressionless as always, carrying the cold dignity that made countless first-year students nervous just by looking at her.","She wore the black suit befitting for academy instructor.","It was none other than Instructor Morgana. She closed the door behind her before walking toward Noah’s bed.","For several seconds, neither of them spoke.","Then, in her usual calm voice, she broke the silence.","\"So... It seems you’ve finally awakened. How are you feeling Noah?\"","Her amethyst eyes quietly met Noah’s.","\"And I imagine you have many questions.\"","Noah watched her with complicated expression. And nodded.","He wanted to ask her... only one question.","It was about Mary"]},{"number":199,"title":"Chapter 199: She’s Gone","paragraphs":["\"I... I’m fine.\"","Noah forced a faint nod before meeting her gaze. \"And yes... I have many questions.\"","Morgana quietly walked toward his bed. She pulled the wooden stool closer and sat beside him with graceful composure, crossing her right leg over her left. Folding her arms beneath her chest, she studied Noah for a brief moment.","The usually cold instructor seemed noticeably quieter today.","Noah hesitated. His lips parted several times before any words came out.","There was only one question that truly mattered. One question he had been terrified to ask ever since he regained consciousness.","He slowly lowered his eyes. \"Instructor Morgana...\"","His voice had become almost a whisper.","\"...Mary.\"","He swallowed the lump forming in his throat. \"Is she... alright?\"","\"...Did you save her?\"","Silence filled the room. It lasted only a few seconds, yet to Noah it felt unbearably long.","Morgana lowered her gaze.","A quiet sigh escaped her lips. \"...I’m truly sorry, Noah. We couldn’t save her.\"","Time seemed to freeze.","Noah’s breathing stopped. His blue eyes widened slightly before all emotion drained from them.","For several long moments, he said nothing.","Slowly he leaned his head back against the pillow and turned his face toward the white ceiling.","\"...I see.\"","His voice was calm. It carried no anger. There was no disbelief.","Morgana quietly watched him before continuing.","\"Everyone else survived. Damien... Kaelan... Ken... Lyria... Arisha...They’re all safe.\"","Noah remained silent.","Morgana continued speaking, her tone calm yet noticeably heavier than before.","\"When we finally reached your location... We found the battlefield completely devastated. There were enormous pillars of ice covering a large section of that place.\"","\"Many trees had been destroyed. The ground itself had shattered. There was also the frozen corpse of a demon.\" She paused briefly.","\"You were lying several meters away. Half of your body had been buried beneath collapsed earth and debris. You had already lost consciousness.\"","Noah quietly listened.","\"We couldn’t find Mary anywhere. So we assumed she had been separated from you.\"","Her expression gradually darkened.","\"When we noticed that the ground beneath you had partially collapsed...We ordered others to dig immediately. They discovered a hidden underground passage.\"","Her eyes lowered.","\"After clearing away the rocks and debris...We found three bodies trapped beneath the collapsed tunnel.\"","Noah slowly closed his eyes.","He already knew what she was about to say.","\"One of them was Mary.\"","The room became silent once again.","\"The other two belonged to human men. They appeared to be around thirty years old. Our investigation confirmed they both were at High Rank of the Condensed Core Realm. They had died beneath the collapse.\"","Noah slowly raised his forearm and covered his eyes.","\"...\"","Not a single word escaped him. A single warm tear slipped from beneath his arm.","It rolled quietly down his cheek before disappearing into the white pillow beneath him.","Morgana’s usually cold expression softened. She reached out without hesitation. Her slender fingers gently brushed through Noah’s soft white hair.","The movement was slow.","\"You shouldn’t blame yourself, Noah.\"","Her voice remained calm.","\"You and Mary did everything you could. You survived against opponents far stronger than yourselves. You fought until the very end.\"","She looked away for a moment.","\"...The responsibility belongs to us. We arrived too late. The Academy failed to protect its students.\"","There was unmistakable guilt within Morgana’s voice.","Noah slowly shook his head. \"...I’m not blaming anyone.\"","His voice trembled slightly.","\"...Not you. Not the Academy. Not even myself.\"","He paused.","Another tear quietly escaped.","\"...I’m just.\"","His lips tightened.","\"...Sad. It hurts.\"","Those two simple words carried more weight than any scream could have.","Morgana said nothing. There were moments when words only made pain heavier.","She continued gently stroking his hair while her other hand quietly found his resting beside the blanket. She wrapped her fingers around his hand with a reassuring grip.","The room remained silent.","Outside the infirmary window, the afternoon breeze gently rustled the leaves of the Academy trees.","---","Several minutes passed in silence.","Noah gradually steadied his breathing. Although the pain in his heart remained, he had finally managed to regain enough composure to speak without his voice trembling.","He took a slow breath before lowering his arm from his eyes.","\"...I’m okay now.\"","His eyes were still slightly red, but he no longer looked as though he would break down at any moment.","Morgana quietly withdrew her hand from his head and released the hand she had been holding. She studied him for a brief moment, making sure he had truly calmed himself.","Noah turned his gaze toward her.","His expression had become much calmer than before, though the sadness lingering in his blue eyes had not disappeared.","\"You probably wanted to ask me some questions...\"","He paused briefly.","\"...About what happened. What we saw. And everything that took place after we separated.\"","Morgana gave a small nod.","\"Yes.\"","Her voice remained gentle.","\"But only if you’re in the right state of mind. \"We can postpone this conversation until tomorrow if necessary.\"","Noah slowly shook his head.","\"No. I’m fine now.\"","A faint smile appeared on his face. Morgana noticed it immediately, but she chose not to point it out. Instead, she simply nodded.","\"Very well.\"","She folded her hands together on her lap.","\"Then tell me everything. Start from the moment you separated from Damien, Kaelan, and Ken. I want every detail you can remember. Nothing is too insignificant. We’re still investigating what happened during the examination.\"","Noah nodded.","\"...Alright.\"","He leaned back against the bed and slowly organized his thoughts.","Then he began.","Morgana listened quietly without interrupting.","Whenever Noah mentioned a spell, an ability, or an unfamiliar detail, she occasionally asked a short question for clarification before allowing him to continue.","When he finished speaking. The room became completely silent.","He didn’t told her about he being on moon and meeting moon goddess.","Nearly half an hour had passed without either of them noticing.","Morgana remained seated in thoughtful silence.","Her calm expression had become far more serious than when the conversation had begun.","She slowly closed the notebook resting on her lap.","\"So...\"","She looked directly into Noah’s eyes.","\"It seems this incident is really complicated. Demons... two unknown explorers. That hidden temple... we found it... but you know what? There was no statue of a woman there, as you told me.\""]},{"number":200,"title":"Chapter 200: Who is she?","paragraphs":["The day after the Incident happened.","Far away from Novaris Academy.","In an unknown location.","Three figures suddenly materialized inside a vast, dimly lit hall. Ripples spread through the surrounding space before quickly fading away.","Click...","The sound of footsteps echoed softly throughout the enormous chamber.","The woman standing at the front began walking forward with calm, measured steps.","Towering white pillars lined both sides of the hall, stretching all the way toward a grand staircase at the far end. Ancient runes glowed faintly upon their surfaces, bathing the chamber in a mysterious crimson light.","Behind the woman, two men silently followed.","One possessed burgundy hair, while the other had dark hair accompanied by a neatly trimmed beard.","They were none other than Boris and Albert.","The woman leading them appeared to be in her early twenties.","She had short black bob-cut hair that framed her delicate face. A pair of round-rimmed glasses rested neatly upon her nose, giving her the appearance of an ordinary scholar rather than someone of great importance.","Her smooth fair skin and emotionless black eyes made her expression impossible to read.","She neither hurried nor slowed her pace.","Every step carried quiet authority. At the end of the hall stood an enormous throne carved from stone.","Beside the staircase that leads to throne waited a young man with dark gray hair and deep brown eyes. Although he appeared to be in his late twenties, the calm discipline in his posture suggested years of unwavering loyalty.","The moment he saw the woman approaching, he immediately knelt on one knee and lowered his head respectfully.","\"Lady Sefira. You have finally returned. I greet you.\"","The woman merely glanced at him.","\"You may rise, Gavin.\"","Her calm voice echoed throughout the silent hall.","Gavin immediately stood.","\"Thank you, my Lady.\"","He stepped aside respectfully as she ascended the wide staircase leading toward the throne.","Boris and Albert also stopped near the foot of the stairs, standing beside Gavin without uttering a single word.","The woman reached the throne before elegantly sitting upon it.","She crossed one leg over the other. A silver ring rested upon the ring finger of her right hand. It looked like a storage ring, but it was not.","Without saying anything, she slowly removed it. The instant the ring left her finger. An overwhelming pressure flooded the entire hall. The atmosphere became unimaginably heavy.","The mana within the surroundings trembled violently.","Even Gavin, Boris, and Albert instinctively lowered their heads.","Cold sweat trickled down their foreheads as their bodies trembled under the terrifying pressure. It wasn’t intentional. It was merely the aura leaking from the woman before them.","\"...Sigh.\"","She let out a quiet breath.","Then after a while her appearance began to change. The short black hair gradually faded into pure snow-white.","It continued growing longer until it flowed gracefully down her back. The ends of her hair slowly transformed into a brilliant orange-red, resembling dancing flames.","Her ordinary black eyes disappeared. In their place emerged radiant amber-gold eyes that burned like living fire.","She removed her glasses as they burned into ashes.","Her fair complexion became almost porcelain-white, flawless beyond comparison.","Even her plain clothing dissolved into particles of light before reforming into an elegant white gown adorned with intricate golden ornaments and crimson gemstones.","Her chest was huge, covered by her white robe while thick thighs hidden underneath.","Every movement she made radiated regal elegance. She no longer resembled an ordinary academy student.","She resembled someone born to rule. Someone standing far above ordinary humans.","Lady Sefira leaned comfortably against the throne.","Everything had returned to its original state.","She calmly spoke. \"Everything proceeded exactly as I had planned.\"","Her burning golden eyes slowly shifted toward the three men standing below.","\"Did you contact Victor? What is the current situation inside the Academy?\"","Gavin respectfully lowered his head.","\"Yes, my Lady. I contacted Victor shortly after everything concluded. The situation has mostly stabilized. All of the invading demons were eliminated except one. His name was Botis.\"","Albert quietly raised an eyebrow before glancing sideways toward Boris.","His expression clearly conveyed one message.","’Isn’t that your brother?’","Boris noticed the look immediately. His eyebrow twitched slightly.","’Shut up. Just because our name is similar doesn’t mean we have connections!’","Albert barely managed to suppress a smile.","Meanwhile, Gavin continued his report without interruption.","\"They have held Botis in custody. While the substitute bodies prepared by Boris and Albert were successfully discovered by the Academy.\"","Gavin paused for a second before continuing, \"The Academy officially confirmed the death of your fake identity...Mary. For all official records, Mary no longer exists. They have accepted her death without suspicion.\"","Sefira silently nodded.","\"And the investigation?\" She asked.","\"The Academy has begun investigating the attack. They currently believe the demons specifically targeted Kaelan Nightfall. They are still trying to determine the motive.\"","\"I see.\"","She rested her chin upon one hand.","\"What about the underground temple?\"","Gavin answered immediately.","\"The Academy discovered it. However, they have yet to uncover its true purpose. They’re still conducting investigations.\"","Silence followed.","Sefira’s thoughts gradually drifted elsewhere.","They went toward a young man with silver-white hair.","A young man who had stood before her without hesitation. Someone who had risked his own life to protect her and fought the demon alone.","She remained silent for several moments before quietly asking,","\"...What about Noah? Is he safe?\"","Gavin nodded.","\"Yes. He survived. His condition is stable. However, he remained unconscious the last time Victor contacted me. He hadn’t awakened yet.\"","Gavin paused briefly.","\"But once he regains consciousness...he’ll most likely report everything he witnessed inside the underground temple. He’ll also mention the statue you have brought from there.\"","Sefira didn’t appear concerned.","\"That’s fine. I never intended to hide the Moon Goddess from the Academy. I intentionally lure Noah inside that temple. I even used some mind magic on him to become more curious. And let him witness death of Mary.\"","She calmly continued,","\"Also there were several demons present. Along with two unknown human infiltrators. If the Academy investigates thoroughly... They’ll most likely conclude that a third hidden party escaped after stealing that statue.\"","She then said, \"And even if they thought something is too weird, they won’t find anything about us.\"","Gavin nodded respectfully.","\"That is the most probable conclusion.\"","\"Excellent.\"","She shifted her gaze toward Boris and Albert.","\"You two also carried out your duties flawlessly. You followed every instruction without error.\"","Her voice remained calm. Yet every word naturally carried unquestionable authority.","The two men immediately bowed deeply. \"It was simply our duty, Boss.\"","\"We only carried out the mission exactly as instructed.\"","\"Very good.\"","Sefira leaned back against the throne. \"Gavin, contact that vampire and tell her we got something related to their goddess.\"","\"Yes, My lady.\" He replied.","\"Now, you are all dismissed.\""]}]);
